{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 120, "key": "FACT-0131: Pricing a second child in the relink is HARMFUL at every penalty tested, and it DESTROYS correct divisions rather than finding them", "observed_at": "2026-08-26", "quote": "Pricing a second child in the relink is HARMFUL at every penalty tested, and it DESTROYS correct divisions rather than finding them", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "INVALID", "validity_reason": "All six sweep arms ran on the leaked substrate (FACT-0160, FACT-0221). \"Penalties never help\" is true only where accepted-fork precision already exceeds break-even, which the leak arranged (10.4% vs 9.0%); on both honest folds the premise INVERTS. The in-run control passed because BOTH sides shared the leak, so it validated the wrong thing. LEVER-0012 is reopened and EXP-0021 re-runs the sweep on OOF split_1 weights. [kb check 2026-09-12: superseded with no successor recorded; retracted rather than left dangling]", "value": "{'fold': 'f1', 'control_score': 0.90542, 'delta_by_penalty': {0: -0.00402, 1: -0.00271, 2: -0.00227, 4: -0.00287, 8: -0.00315}, 'div_tp_by_penalty': {'control': 26, 0: 22, 1: 21, 2: 21, 4: 21, 8: 23}}"}
