{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 124, "key": "FACT-0150: GT annotates only 5.4% of cells, so our division over-emission is 2.65x per cell-per-frame, NOT the ~50x the raw 6,314-vs-125 comparison implies", "observed_at": "2026-08-26", "quote": "GT annotates only 5.4% of cells, so our division over-emission is 2.65x per cell-per-frame, NOT the ~50x the raw 6,314-vs-125 comparison implies", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The counts behind the ratio (TP 26 / FP 225 / 251 scored / 6,314 forks) come from the VOID EXP-0019 (FACT-0160). The STRUCTURE survives and is ground truth - GT annotates only 5.4% of cells, so any raw forks-vs-GT-divisions ratio overstates over-emission - but 2.65 itself must be re-derived on honest weights before it is cited as a number.", "value": "2.65 over_emission_ratio"}
