{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 126, "key": "FACT-0152: Division-filter break-even - keeping fraction a of TP and b of FP improves divJ only if a > 0.357 + 0.643 b", "observed_at": "2026-08-26", "quote": "Division-filter break-even - keeping fraction a of TP and b of FP improves divJ only if a > 0.357 + 0.643 b", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "INVALID", "validity_reason": "The algebra is sound but its coefficients are pure functions of the leaked TP=26 / FP=225 / 125 split from the VOID EXP-0019 (FACT-0160). Re-costed on honest counts by FACT-0171, break-even is 616 false divisions removed per true one lost on fold 1 - not the 1.56 implied here. The qualitative conclusion (proportional pruning is harmful) survives in FACT-0171; the numbers 0.357 and 0.643 do not. [kb check 2026-09-12: superseded with no successor recorded; retracted rather than left dangling]", "value": ""}
