{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 371, "key": "1_rules", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "##ENTRY IN THIS COMPETITION CONSTITUTES YOUR ACCEPTANCE OF THESE OFFICIAL COMPETITION RULES.\n\n**[See Section 3.18 for defined terms](rules#18.-terms)**\n\n*The Competition named below is a skills-based competition to promote and further the field of data science. You must register via the Competition Website to enter. To enter the Competition, you must agree to these Official Competition Rules, whic", "review_after": null, "source_id": 2, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "36507 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/1_rules.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 372, "key": "2_Description", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Tracking cells across time in 3D microscopy is a fundamental challenge in biological research. Scientists rely on time-lapse 3D imaging to study how cells grow, interact, and evolve, but analyzing this data remains a massive bottleneck. Currently, researchers spend countless hours manually tracking cells—especially in complex datasets where thousands of visually similar cells move, deform, and div", "review_after": null, "source_id": 3, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "1068 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/2_Description.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 373, "key": "3_Evaluation", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Submissions are evaluated using a combined tracking metric that measures both edge accuracy (how well cells are linked across time) and division detection (how well cell mitosis events are identified). The combined score is:\n  \n  $$\\text{score} = \\text{adjusted_edge_jaccard} + 0.1 \\times \\text{division_jaccard}$$\n\nEdge Jaccard: Predicted nodes are matched to ground-truth nodes per timepoint via op", "review_after": null, "source_id": 4, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "2390 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/3_Evaluation.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 374, "key": "4_Timeline", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "* **June 29, 2026** - Start Date. \n* **September 22, 2026** - Entry Deadline. You must accept the competition rules before this date in order to compete. \n* **September 22, 2026** - Team Merger Deadline. This is the last day participants may join or merge teams. \n* **September 29, 2026** - Final Submission Deadline. \n\nAll deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC on the corresponding day unless otherwise note", "review_after": null, "source_id": 5, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "505 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/4_Timeline.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 375, "key": "5_data-description", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "## Dataset Description\n\nEach sample in this dataset is a short 3D+time video of fluorescently labeled zebrafish embryo cells, stored as a [Zarr v3](https://zarr-specs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/v3/core/v3.0.html) volume. Your task is to detect cells in each timepoint and link them across time, producing a tracking graph of nodes (cell detections) and edges (temporal links between cells).\n\n### Data F", "review_after": null, "source_id": 6, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "2296 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/5_data-description.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 376, "key": "6_Prizes", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "* 1st Place - $18,000\n* 2nd Place - $12,000\n* 3rd Place - $8,000\n* 4th Place - $6,000\n* 5th Place - $6,000\n* 6th Place - $5,000\n* 7th Place - $5,000", "review_after": null, "source_id": 7, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "148 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/6_Prizes.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 377, "key": "7_Code_Requirements", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "<img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-media/competitions/general/Kerneler-white-desc2_transparent.png\" style=\"float: right; width: 70px; padding: 10px\">\n\nSubmissions to this competition must be made through Notebooks. In order for the \"Submit\" button to be active after a commit, the following conditions must be met: \n- CPU Notebook <= 12 hours run-time \n- GPU Notebook <= 12 hours run-tim", "review_after": null, "source_id": 8, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "835 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/7_Code_Requirements.md"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 378, "key": "8_abstract", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Your goal is to develop algorithms to detect, track and link cells across time in 3D microscopy data, including accurate identification of cell divisions and lineage reconstruction. You will work with real microscopy datasets to build robust methods that can handle dense cell populations, noise and complex biological structures.\n\nYour work will eliminate a massive manual bottleneck in biological r", "review_after": null, "source_id": 9, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "page", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "465 chars @ evidence/raw/pages/8_abstract.md"}
