{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 422, "key": "division_term_is_the_gap (SUPERSEDED 2026-09-11: The plateau already scores divJ ~0.231, so the gap to rank 1 is not 'the entire division term'. Headroom is near-equal: edge +0.074, division +0.077. Divisions remain the better lever only because the field's tuning leaves divJ frozen.)", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "score = adjusted_edge_jaccard + w * division_jaccard, with w = 0.1", "review_after": null, "source_id": null, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 1112, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "Legacy fact has no source or quote; recover the original evidence before relying on it", "value": "The 0.0235 gap between the 0.9465 public plateau and rank 1 (0.970) divided by the 0.1 division weight implies division_jaccard ~ 0.235 at rank 1. A competitor reported measuring 0.22 (topic 739516) and a one-to-one linker scores 0.000 (topic 733877). So the plateau is teams with working EDGES and ZERO divisions; the entire podium gap is the division term. This is an honest, defensible lever - no metric gaming required."}
