{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 430, "key": "F-0001: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Biohub-X is a standalone Git repository with no ancestor repository; no tracked file names a quarantined prior-campaign repository; no tracked file carries an absolute filesystem path outside the allow-listed provenance records; and no import-path entry resolves outside the repository, its virtual e", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Repository-isolation contract; the blind-isolation rule was dissolved 2026-09-07."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 431, "key": "F-0002: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The two content identities separate platform drift from content change: a CRLF rewrite of a configuration file breaks its raw identity and leaves its canonical identity intact, while a single-character content edit breaks both.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CRLF/canonical digest behaviour - an implementation detail of a system we are porting wholesale."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 432, "key": "F-0003: Unmatched predicted nodes are NOT edge false positives. Sets the whole economics of detection precision.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Under the pinned official scorer, a predicted node that matches no ground-truth node adds no edge false positive. Adding one isolated, unmatched node to a perfect two-node prediction left edge TP, FP, FN at 1, 0, 0 and the raw edge Jaccard at 1.0. An edge between two mutually unmatched predicted nodes is likewise uncharged. The exemption ends at the annotated cells: an edge whose source matches a ground-truth node that has a ground-truth successor, but which points elsewhere, was charged as one false positive."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 433, "key": "F-0004: Node-count adjustment is clamped only at zero, so the multiplier exceeds 1 when under-predicting. Measured 1.09.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The official node-count adjustment multiplies the edge Jaccard by 1 - 0.1 * (N_pred - N_total) / N_total and is clamped only at zero, so the multiplier exceeds one whenever fewer nodes are predicted than the estimated total. With 2 predicted nodes, a declared estimated total of 20 and a raw edge Jaccard of 1.0, total_node_ratio was -0.9 and the adjusted edge Jaccard was 1.09."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 434, "key": "F-0005: Frame-skipping edges are silently DROPPED by the scorer, not charged. Affects gap-recovery designs.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The two boundaries around a multi-frame edge behave differently and were measured separately. The Biohub-X lineage contract refuses an edge that does not advance exactly one frame at construction, so such an edge cannot reach evaluation. The pinned official scorer, called directly on a graph built beneath that contract, drops a frame-skipping edge instead of charging it: a prediction whose only edge ran from frame 0 to frame 2 produced edge TP 0, FP 0 and FN 2 against a ground truth of two consecutive edges."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 435, "key": "F-0006: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A complete detect-to-score chain can be run on a deterministic synthetic fixture with no competition data, no GPU and no external artifact, and the graph it emits is legal by construction. On the default fixture the chain detects 14 instances, offers 37 candidate edges at a 12 micrometre radius, rea", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Synthetic-fixture vertical slice; superseded by the real-data findings."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 436, "key": "F-0007: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Candidate reach is a real ceiling on the edge Jaccard and its two failure modes are separately attributable. Narrowing the candidate radius to 1 micrometre, below the fixture's one-to-two micrometre true displacements, dropped reach to 0.182 with 9 true edges unreachable outside the radius and 0 unr", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Fixture-scale candidate-reach demo; the corpus-wide versions (F-0026..F-0032) supersede it."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 437, "key": "F-0008: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The node-count lever measured on hand-built graphs in F-0003 and F-0004 reproduces through a whole running pipeline. Between fixture noise 0.06 and 0.15 the detector went from 15 to 189 instances while the raw edge Jaccard stayed at 0.9091 and edge false positives stayed at 0; the node-count ratio r", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Fixture reproduction of F-0003/F-0004; the corpus-wide F-0015/F-0018 are the usable versions."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 438, "key": "F-0009: An edgeless graph is UNSCORABLE - evaluate() returns early and raises. A graph with no edges is a bug, not a low score.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/end_to_end/test_vertical_slice.py | 19 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A prediction that abstains on every target emits a graph with nodes and no edges, and the pinned official scorer cannot score it: `evaluate` returns early for an edgeless graph without applying its matching, so the `node_recall` helper it documents as requiring a matched graph raises a KeyError from inside tracksdata rather than returning a number. Biohub-X refuses such a prediction with a named error instead."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 439, "key": "F-0010: The visible test split is 4 volumes, byte-identical to train, verified by tree digest. Never select on it.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_competition_corpus.py | 6 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The local test split is not a held-out evaluation set. It contains four volumes and no ground truth at all, and every one of the four is byte-identical to a train volume carrying the same dataset id, confirmed by matching tree digests over 456,757,564 to 547,662,847 bytes each. It is a format example for the submission pipeline; the genuinely held-out data is the hidden set swapped in at rerun."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 440, "key": "F-0011: 199 datasets are 2 embryos, not 199 subjects: 6bba has 128 fields of view, 44b6 has 71.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_competition_corpus.py | 6 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The supervised corpus spans two embryos, not 199 independent subjects. Dataset ids are {embryo}_{field_of_view}, and the 199 annotated train datasets divide into embryo 6bba with 128 fields of view and embryo 44b6 with 71."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 441, "key": "F-0012: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Annotation is sparse by orders of magnitude. Across the 199 annotated train datasets the ground truth totals 2,353,863 bytes against 87,607,537,865 bytes of volume, which is 0.0027 percent. Per dataset the median ground truth is 11,713 bytes against a median volume of 411,186,738 bytes.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Superseded by F-0013, which measures annotated fraction properly rather than by byte size."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 442, "key": "F-0013: 133,318 annotated nodes / 128,883 edges against 4,725,117 estimated - 2.82% annotated, ranging 0.13-20.21% per dataset.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 199 datasets surveyed, all carrying an estimate", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Annotation density varies by two orders of magnitude across the corpus and differs systematically between the two embryos. Across 199 annotated datasets there are 133,318 annotated nodes and 128,883 annotated edges against a summed estimated_number_of_nodes of 4,725,117, so 2.821 percent overall. Per dataset the annotated fraction ranges from 0.13 to 20.21 percent with a median of 3.56. Embryo 44b6 has a median density of 0.77 percent across 71 movies; embryo 6bba has 9.71 percent across 128."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 443, "key": "F-0014: DIVISION SCARCITY: 151 annotated divisions in the whole corpus; 112 of 199 datasets have none. LOEO trains divisions on 26 (44b6) or 125 (6bba) examples.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 151 divisions across 199 datasets", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Division supervision is extremely scarce. The corpus contains 151 annotated divisions in total, and 112 of the 199 datasets contain none at all. The median dataset has zero and the maximum has five. Embryo 44b6 holds 26 divisions and embryo 6bba holds 125, so a leave-one-embryo-out fold trains a division model on either 26 or 125 examples."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 444, "key": "F-0015: Predicting the ANNOTATED count rather than the estimated total yields a median multiplier of 1.0964 (range 1.0798-1.0999).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 199 datasets, medians 1.0000 / 1.0929 / 1.0964 / 1.0982", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The official node-count adjustment offers roughly a ten percent uplift on the raw edge Jaccard to a system that predicts the annotated node count rather than the true cell count. Using each dataset's own estimated_number_of_nodes, the multiplier 1 - 0.1 * (N_pred - N_total) / N_total has a median of 1.0000 when predicting the estimated total and 1.0964 when predicting the annotated count, ranging 1.0798 to 1.0999. It is 1.0992 for embryo 44b6 and 1.0903 for embryo 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 445, "key": "F-0016: The division counter shares the unmatched-prediction exemption: an all-unmatched fork is uncharged but still raises num_pred_nodes.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 13 passed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The official division counter shares the unmatched-prediction exemption that F-0003 measured for edges. A predicted fork built entirely from unmatched nodes is not charged: added to a perfect single-division prediction it left division TP, FP, FN at 1, 0, 0 and the division Jaccard at 1.0, while raising num_pred_nodes from 3 to 6 and lowering the adjusted edge Jaccard from 1.0 to 0.9. The exemption ends at the annotated cells: against a ground truth holding no divisions, a fork whose own node matched an annotated cell with a successor was charged as one division false positive, taking the division Jaccard from undefined to 0.0, and was charged again as one edge false positive."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 446, "key": "F-0017: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The Phase-2 chain runs end to end on real competition bytes and scores 0.082121 through the pinned official scorer, and detection rather than association is what limits it. On a 12-frame, 32x128x128 window of 6bba_2540cd90 holding 26 annotated nodes and 22 annotated edges, the classical local-maximu", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "An 0.082 score from the first real-data chain - an obsolete baseline, and its lesson is restated in F-0025."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 447, "key": "F-0018: THE ECONOMICS OF THE NODE-COUNT LEVER: worth ~9% of adjusted edge Jaccard, and it stops paying once a filter destroys more than ~8% of correct edges.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate retention | artifacts/retention-oracle.json, 199 datasets, 1180 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Emitting the annotated node count instead of the estimated cell count is worth about nine percent of the adjusted edge Jaccard, and it stops paying once a filter destroys more than about eight percent of the correct edges to get there. Across all 199 annotated training datasets, a dense prediction padded to each dataset's own estimated_number_of_nodes scored an adjusted edge Jaccard of exactly 1.0000 on both embryo folds, because its node ratio is zero by construction. The same edges emitted at the annotated node count scored 1.0986 on 44b6 and 1.0905 on 6bba. Sweeping the fraction of correct edges the filtered policy retains, both folds break even at 0.92 and both fall behind the dense baseline at 0.90, by 0.0114 on 44b6 and 0.0184 on 6bba. Reaching 0.014 above the dense baseline, which is the step from a 0.936 system to 0.950 with the division term held fixed, requires a retention of 0.94 on both folds: 0.0327 on 44b6 and 0.0251 on 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 448, "key": "F-0019: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A three-valued detection target with an intensity-quantile ignore band keeps every annotated cell supervised while refusing to call unannotated cells background, and the whole E03 training loop runs on CPU. On the E01 window at the ninetieth percentile the target was 26 positive, 353,632 negative an", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Superseded by F-0020, then F-0021."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 449, "key": "F-0020: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "No intensity band can call any voxel background without contradicting annotated cells, and the failure is not a grid artefact. Measuring the intensity percentile of 5,291 annotated nodes across all 199 training movies, the dimmest annotated cell sits at percentile 0.5263 on 44b6 and 0.0917 on 6bba. ", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Superseded by F-0021, which audits every node rather than a sample."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 450, "key": "F-0021: NO intensity band can call any voxel background: the dimmest annotated cell sits at percentile 0.09. Audited over all 133,318 nodes, zero excluded.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate mask-audit | artifacts/mask-audit.json, 199 datasets, 133,318 nodes, 1699 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Audited over every annotated node in the corpus rather than a sample, no intensity band survives on either fold, the class prior is valid at every scale, and no annotated cell is lost to the model grid. All 133,318 annotated nodes across 18,933 annotated frames were measured, with zero excluded by sampling and zero falling outside the strided grid, so coverage is exact. The dimmest annotated cell sits at percentile 0.2987 on 44b6 and 0.0628 on 6bba, so band selection returns nothing for BOTH folds, not only 6bba: the q50 band that appeared to survive on 44b6 under four-frame sampling does not survive the full population. The q90 band would call 4,877 of 20,197 44b6 nodes (24.1 percent) and 16,336 of 113,121 6bba nodes (14.4 percent) background. Grid collisions are zero, so the count of positive voxels equals the annotated node count exactly. The class prior spans 1.443e-4 to 3.000e-3 per grid voxel with a median of 6.832e-4, every dataset inside the open unit interval. Annotated cells are local intensity maxima for 12.0 percent of 44b6 and 6.1 percent of 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 451, "key": "F-0022: The SCAR assumption nnPU relies on is NOT supported: annotation density correlates with annotated-cell intensity at Pearson r=+0.354. Densely annotated movies carry BRIGHTER annotations.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate mask-audit | artifacts/mask-audit.json, selection_bias_probe, 199 datasets", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The SCAR assumption that nnPU relies on is not supported by this corpus. Across the 199 training datasets, annotation density correlates with the median intensity percentile of the annotated cells at Pearson r = +0.354. Labelling is therefore not independent of the feature the detector reads, and the direction is that densely annotated movies carry brighter annotations, not dimmer ones."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 452, "key": "F-0023: Minimum-track-length filtering with isolated-node pruning is near-free: 0.9963 / 0.9945 edge retention at span 6, with the division exemption.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate track-length | artifacts/track-length.json, 199 datasets, 133,318 nodes, 30.5 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A minimum-track-length filter with isolated-node pruning is nearly free in correct edges and nearly inert in node count when applied to the annotated graphs. Sweeping the minimum frame span over all 199 annotated training datasets, with the division exemption the public notebooks carry, edge retention at the span of 6 those notebooks use is 0.9963 on 44b6 and 0.9945 on 6bba, against the 0.94 target and 0.92 break-even F-0018 established. Every span from 2 to 10 clears both bars on both folds; even a span of 10 retains 0.9875 and 0.9763. Node retention tracks it closely, 0.9945 and 0.9928 at span 6, so the filter removes between 0.5 and 0.7 percent of annotated nodes. Dropping the division exemption changes retention by less than 0.002 anywhere in the sweep."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 453, "key": "F-0024: NOT INGESTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The clean-fold nnPU training loop runs end to end on a real Kaggle T4 with every guard intact. On fold_44b6 with two 44b6 movies, two epochs, seed 4460, batch size 2 and learning rate 1e-4, the masked positive-unlabelled risk fell from 0.61999181 to 0.60510752 across two epochs of two batches each, ", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "retracted", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "bx-skipped", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Process check that the nnPU loop runs on a T4; F-0022 undermines the nnPU premise anyway."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 454, "key": "F-0025: Multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians dominates the classical local-max detector at a matched proposal budget (0.6154 vs 0.3846 reach).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx.proposals.dog, measured against biohubx.proposals.classical | 26 annotated nodes, window estimated cells 56.7; classical 75 / 0.3846 and 310 / 0.7692; DoG 20 / 0.1923, 44 / 0.4231, 58 / 0.5000, 73 / 0.6154, 104 / 0.6538, 228 / 0.7308, 483 / 1.0000", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians proposal source on the isotropic grid dominates the classical local-maximum detector on the recall-versus-budget frontier, on the F-0017 window. At a matched proposal budget the classical detector at threshold 0.70 emits 75 proposals and reaches 0.3846 annotated nodes within the official 7 micrometre radius, while DoG at response quantile 0.997 emits 73 and reaches 0.6154. At matched reachability the classical detector needs 310 proposals for 0.7692 while DoG needs 228 for 0.7308. DoG reaches 1.0000 at 483 proposals, which is 8.51 times the window's estimated cell count and carries a node-count multiplier of 0.2488."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 455, "key": "F-0026: DoG reaches roughly TWICE the annotated cells of the classical detector, on both embryos, at every budget swept.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals | artifacts/proposals.json, 199 movies, 0 skipped, 491.9 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians proposal source reaches roughly twice as many annotated cells as the classical local-maximum detector, on both embryos, at every node budget swept. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, covering 394 annotated nodes on 44b6 and 1,762 on 6bba, reachability at the neutral budget of one times the estimated cell count is 0.7614 against 0.3528 on 44b6 and 0.6288 against 0.3610 on 6bba. Selecting the budget on one embryo and freezing it before measuring the other, both folds improve: fold_44b6 selects ratio 2.0 and reads 0.7770 against 0.4523 on held-out 6bba, and fold_6bba selects ratio 2.0 and reads 0.7944 against 0.3629 on held-out 44b6. At the one point where the two sources emit almost the same number of proposals, 6bba with classical at 31,045 and DoG at 31,482, DoG reaches 0.5539 against 0.4523."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 456, "key": "F-0027: Reachability plateaus on 44b6 and still climbs on 6bba out to 8x the estimated cell count; one-to-one node recall tracks reach within 0.01.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses | artifacts/proposals-e04b.json, 199 movies, 2,033 nodes audited, 654.6 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Extending the DoG budget sweep to eight times the estimated cell count, the reachability curve plateaus on 44b6 and is still rising slowly on 6bba, and one-to-one node recall tracks reachability to within 0.01 everywhere. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, DoG reaches 0.8046 at the neutral budget on 44b6 and 0.8807 from ratio 6 onward, where it emits about 87,000 proposals against an allowance of 336,000 and cannot fill the budget; on 6bba it reaches 0.6385 at the neutral budget, 0.9001 at ratio 6 and 0.9092 at ratio 8. The classical detector saturates at 0.3629 and 0.4546 from ratio 2 onward on the same movies. Selecting the budget on one embryo and measuring the other, fold_44b6 reads 0.9001 against 0.4546 and fold_6bba reads 0.8807 against 0.3629. Auditing the 2,033 annotated nodes at the neutral budget, the 69 missed on 44b6 and 617 missed on 6bba sit at median intensity percentile 0.919 and 0.955 within their frame against 0.988 and 0.994 for reached nodes, at median DoG response percentile 0.915 and 0.969 against 0.989 and 0.997, with no difference in annotated crowding or boundary distance, and with a proposal already lying within 14 micrometres of 87 percent of 44b6 misses and 50 percent of 6bba misses."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 457, "key": "F-0028: Residual misses differ by embryo: on 44b6 it is a LOCALISATION failure, not a detection failure - a proposal already lies within 10um of 73% of missed cells.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses --audit-ratio 8.0 | artifacts/proposals-residual-r8.json, 2,033 nodes audited, 450.9 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The annotated cells DoG still misses at eight times the estimated cell count are two different populations on the two embryos. On 44b6 the residual is 44 of 365 nodes (12.1 percent) and is a localisation failure: the missed cells have median intensity percentile 0.897 within their frame with none below 0.50, median DoG response percentile 0.888, and a proposal already lies within 10 micrometres of 73 percent of them and within 14 of 93 percent, at a median nearest distance of 9.08 micrometres, just outside the official 7 micrometre radius. On 6bba the residual is 160 of 1,668 nodes (9.6 percent) and is half dimness: 60 percent sit below intensity percentile 0.80 and 10 percent below 0.50, median DoG response percentile 0.877, with a proposal within 10 micrometres of 44 percent and within 14 of 78 percent. On neither embryo do annotated crowding within 10 micrometres (4.5 and 1.3 percent) or proximity to a volume face (16 percent within 5 micrometres on both) distinguish the residual from reached cells."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 458, "key": "F-0029: The near-miss residual is in-plane, not a z artefact: median in-plane offset 7.46/7.85um against median |z| 3.25/4.88.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses, with the nearest-proposal displacement recorded | artifacts/proposals-residual-r8-displacement.json, 2,033 nodes audited, 613.5 seconds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The near-miss residual is not sub-voxel error and not a z artefact. Among the annotated cells DoG still misses at eight times the estimated cell count whose nearest proposal lies within 14 micrometres, 41 on 44b6 and 125 on 6bba, the displacement from cell to nearest proposal is dominated by the plane: median in-plane offset 7.46 and 7.85 micrometres against median absolute z offset 3.25 and 4.88, with z the larger component for only 29 and 22 percent. The signed z offset has no consistent direction, mean +0.83 and -1.05 micrometres, so there is no systematic depth bias. The in-plane offset's interquartile range, 5.8 to 8.9 on 44b6 and 6.4 to 9.8 on 6bba, is the spacing between neighbouring nuclei on a grid whose plane step is 1.625 micrometres."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 459, "key": "F-0030: Greedy physical-radius suppression does NOT return local maxima - it packs the above-threshold region. Only 46 of 686 accepted points were strict 26-neighbourhood maxima.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx.proposals.dog against scipy.ndimage.maximum_filter, one frame | 686 accepted, 46 peaks, 6.7 percent; identical counts across three banks", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Greedy physical-radius suppression does not return local maxima; it packs the above-threshold region, and on this data most of what it returns are shoulders of blobs. On frame 0 of 6bba_2540cd90 at the 0.95 response quantile, 13,108 of 262,144 strided voxels cleared the threshold, the suppression pass accepted 686 of them at a 4 micrometre radius, and only 46 of those 686 are strict 26-neighbourhood maxima of the response, against 37.8 estimated cells in the frame. Three different scale banks, (2.0, 3.0, 4.5), (2.0, 3.0) and (2.0, 2.5, 3.0), returned exactly 1,398 candidates on the same two-frame window, because the count is set by how much of the frame clears the quantile rather than by how many blobs there are."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 460, "key": "F-0031: DoG BANK TUNING: dropping the 4.5um scale RAISES reachability on 44b6 everywhere; adding 2.5um changes nothing. Use (2.0, 3.0).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --radii | artifacts/proposals-h11b-r23.json, artifacts/proposals-h11b-r2253.json", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Removing the 4.5 micrometre scale from the DoG bank raises reachability on 44b6 at every budget and at every matched proposal count, and on 6bba only above twice the estimated cell count; adding a 2.5 micrometre scale changes nothing. Over all 199 annotated movies under the packed suppression regime of F-0027, the (2.0, 3.0) bank reaches 0.8782 against 0.8046 on 44b6 at the neutral budget, 0.9543 against 0.8680 at twice it, and plateaus at 0.9695 against 0.8807; at the baseline's own proposal counts it reads 0.9371 against 0.8680 and 0.9570 against 0.8756. On 6bba it reads 0.5936 against 0.6385 at the neutral budget, 0.7980 against 0.8093 at twice it, and at the baseline's count there 0.7796 against 0.8093, before overtaking at four times, 0.9115 against 0.8865, and eight, 0.9427 against 0.9092. The (2.0, 2.5, 3.0) bank matches (2.0, 3.0) to four decimals at every point. Selecting on one embryo and measuring the other, fold_44b6 reads 0.9115 and fold_6bba reads 0.9695 with the two-scale bank, against 0.9001 and 0.8807 with three scales."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 461, "key": "F-0032: BEST MEASURED DETECTOR: strict 26-neighbourhood maxima on a (2.0,3.0)um DoG bank reaches 0.9239 (44b6) / 0.8984 (6bba) while emitting at or below the estimated cell count.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --local-maxima --radii 2.0,3.0 | artifacts/proposals-peaks-r23.json, artifacts/proposals-peaks-r2345.json", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Requiring a DoG candidate to be a strict 26-neighbourhood maximum, with the two-scale bank (2.0, 3.0) micrometres, reaches 0.9239 of annotated cells on 44b6 and 0.8984 on 6bba while emitting at or below the estimated cell count, and does so with a third to a half of the proposals the packed detector needed to reach less. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, the peaks detector saturates at 43,825 proposals on 44b6 against a neutral budget of 56,032, and at 50,159 on 6bba against 42,309; at the neutral budget it reads 0.9213 with 42,478 proposals on 44b6 and 0.7894 with 37,417 on 6bba, and at twice it 0.9239 and 0.8933. The packed detector with the three-scale bank, interpolated to the peaks detector's own proposal counts, reads 0.7159 on 44b6 and 0.6803 on 6bba. Under the peaks rule the large scale hurts on both embryos above the neutral budget: three scales saturate at 0.7665 and 0.8314 with 26,847 and 32,544 proposals, because neighbouring nuclei merge into one maximum at 4.5 micrometres; at the neutral budget on 6bba alone the three-scale bank still edges the two-scale one, 0.8048 against 0.7894. Selecting the budget on one embryo and measuring the other with the two-scale peaks detector, fold_44b6 reads 0.8933 on held-out 6bba at twice the estimate and fold_6bba reads 0.9239 on held-out 44b6 at four times it, against classical 0.4523 and 0.3629. The remaining misses at the neutral budget are 31 of 365 on 44b6, every one within 14 micrometres of a proposal and 84 percent within 10, and 368 of 1,668 on 6bba, of which 30 percent sit below intensity percentile 0.80 and 64 percent lie within 14 micrometres of a proposal."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 462, "key": "F-0033: ORACLE ASSOCIATION CEILING: with ground-truth-chosen edges over frozen strict peaks, 0.9961 on 44b6 but only 0.9227 on 6bba. Detection is still the binding constraint on 6bba.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate oracle-ceiling | artifacts/e06-oracle.json", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Over the frozen strict-peak proposals of D-0041, a legal graph whose edges are chosen with ground truth scores 0.9961 on 44b6 and 0.9227 on 6bba through the pinned official scorer, on ten-frame windows of all 199 annotated training movies. The 44b6 ceiling clears 0.950 and the 6bba ceiling does not, so under E06's preregistered rule association is not yet the sole bottleneck and the bake-off does not start. On 44b6, 1,811 of 1,970 annotated nodes matched a proposal one-to-one within 7 micrometres (0.9193), 1,544 of 1,750 annotated edges survived with both endpoints matched (0.8823), both retained divisions were kept, and 219,020 proposals stood against an estimated 280,156, a node ratio of -0.2182 that the official adjustment rewards: raw edge Jaccard 0.8823, adjusted 0.8961, division Jaccard 1.0. On 6bba, 9,208 of 10,157 nodes matched (0.9066), 7,852 of 8,949 edges survived (0.8774), 7 of 9 divisions were kept, and 275,566 proposals stood against an estimated 211,565, a node ratio of +0.3025 that the adjustment charges: raw edge Jaccard 0.8781, adjusted 0.8449, division Jaccard 0.7778. One 6bba window with 9 annotated edges retained no edge and could not be scored. The same detector configuration therefore under-proposes the sparse embryo by a fifth and over-proposes the dense one by a third; at a zero node ratio the 6bba ceiling would read 0.9559 and the 44b6 ceiling 0.9823, so the 6bba shortfall is proposal count before it is edge retention."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 463, "key": "F-0034: Per-scale strict peaks unioned before one shared suppression recovers what max-over-scales fusion loses; whether it helps depends entirely on the bank.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --per-scale-union | artifacts/proposals-h11c-union-r2345.json, artifacts/proposals-h11d-union-r23.json", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Taking strict peaks at each DoG scale on its own and unioning them before one shared suppression pass (H-11c) recovers what the max-over-scales response loses to fusion, and whether that helps depends entirely on the bank. With the three-scale bank (2.0, 3.0, 4.5) the union saturates at 0.8376 reach on 44b6 with 37,596 proposals and 0.8842 on 6bba with 46,273, above the fused three-scale peaks (0.7665 and 0.8314) and below the frozen two-scale peaks (0.9239 and 0.8984), so the 4.5 micrometre scale costs more than fusion does. With the frozen two-scale bank (2.0, 3.0), H-11d, the union saturates at 0.9467 on 44b6 with 50,642 proposals and 0.9291 on 6bba with 60,587, above the frozen peaks by 0.023 and 0.031, and both held-out directions improve: fold_44b6 reads 0.9064 on held-out 6bba at twice the estimate against 0.8933, fold_6bba reads 0.9467 on held-out 44b6 at four times it against 0.9239. The gain is bought with proposals: the union emits 16 percent more on 44b6 and 21 percent more on 6bba at saturation, and at the neutral budget on the dense embryo it reads 0.7440 with 39,706 proposals against the frozen peaks' 0.7894 with 37,417, so its extra candidates outrank true cells there. On 44b6 at the neutral budget the two are level, 0.9188 against 0.9213."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 464, "key": "F-0035: Truncating proposals to a budget chosen on the TRAINING embryo does not raise the held-out ceiling; the per-scale union without truncation does.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate oracle-ceiling --budget-ratios, with and without --per-scale-union | artifacts/e05-peaks.json, artifacts/e05-union.json", "review_after": null, "source_id": 47, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Truncating proposals to a budget chosen on the training embryo does not raise the oracle ceiling on the held-out embryo, and the per-scale union without truncation does. Over ten-frame windows of all 199 annotated movies, arm A0 (the frozen D-0041 peaks, untruncated) reproduces F-0033 exactly at 0.9961 on 44b6 and 0.9227 on 6bba, which is the check that the instrument change did not move the baseline. Budgeted selection is killed on its own falsifier: fold_44b6 selects k=1.5 on 44b6 (0.9962 against A0's 0.9961) and reads 0.9072 on held-out 6bba against A0's 0.9227, and the union arm A3 selects the same ratio and reads 0.9116, also below A0. Only the direction that selects on the dense embryo improves, and only trivially: fold_6bba picks k=2.0 and reads 0.9961 on held-out 44b6, equal to A0 to four decimals. Arm A2, the per-scale union with no truncation and therefore no constant to select, improves both directions at once: 1.0195 on 44b6 against 0.9961 and 0.9283 on 6bba against 0.9227. It buys that with proposals, 253,543 and 330,820 against 219,020 and 275,566, and pays the node-ratio charge on the dense embryo, +0.5637 against +0.3025, while raising its node match fraction from 0.9066 to 0.9300 and its edge retention from 0.8774 to 0.9107. No arm reaches 0.950 on 6bba; the best held-out reading on that embryo is A2's 0.9283."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 465, "key": "measured_divJ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "| **pooled** | **11,582** | **5** | **613** | **146** | **151** | **0.0065** |", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Pooled LOEO division Jaccard was 0.0065 (fold 44b6 0.0152, fold 6bba 0.0047): 11,582 forks emitted, 5 TP, 613 FP, 146 FN against 151 GT divisions."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 466, "key": "fp_and_fn_are_disjoint", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The 613 FP forks and the 146 FN divisions are disjoint populations. Re-ranking, filtering, or re-scoring the forks we already emit recovers exactly ZERO divisions - the fork is never in the right place to begin with.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "DECISIVE: of the 146 FN divisions, ZERO have a fork emitted at the matched mother, in both folds. Re-ranking, filtering or re-scoring the forks we already emit recovers exactly ZERO divisions. Precision work cannot add a single TP."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 467, "key": "root_cause_gates", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The deployed division proposer's sister-distance gate (7.2 um) sits below the GT median inter-daughter distance in both embryos (8.98 / 11.47 um). We are not ranking true divisions badly - we are refusing to propose them.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE BUG: the fork proposer's gates are mis-set against measured GT geometry. SAFE_DIV_MAX_UM=4.7 vs GT median parent-daughter 5.7-6.4um (p90 8.4-9.9); SAFE_DIV_SISTER_MAX_UM=7.2 vs GT median inter-daughter 8.98um (44b6) / 11.47um (6bba). The gate excludes the MEDIAN true division. Located at src/biotrack/wrapper.py:123-127."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 468, "key": "ranking_is_backwards", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "it ranks the tightest pairs first, i.e. exactly backwards with respect to the measured GT geometry", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 488, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The proposer's ranking score = parent_dist + 0.15*sister_dist (wrapper.py:831) is monotonically INCREASING in both distances, so it ranks tightest pairs first - exactly backwards. True divisions are the wide, angularly-opposed, persistently-diverging ones."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 469, "key": "gate_widening_table", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "| 15.0 | 33 | **81** |  ... raising both to (15, 10) admits 81 of 89 - an 8x increase in what is even proposable.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Widening both gates to (sister 15, parent 10) raises admissible divisions from 10 to 81 of the 89 metric-reachable - an 8x increase. Both gates must move: raising sister alone saturates at 33/89 because the parent gate then binds."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 470, "key": "postproc_ceiling", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "**[MEASURED] 84 of 151 divisions (55.6 %) are recoverable by post-processing alone** ... the post-processing ceiling is 89/151 = 0.589 divJ.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "84 of 151 divisions (55.6%) are recoverable by POST-PROCESSING ALONE - mother and both daughters are already detected and matched, only the second mother-daughter edge is missing. With the 5 existing TPs the post-processing ceiling is 89/151 = 0.589 divJ."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 471, "key": "public_field_inherited_the_bug (SUPERSEDED: true of the 0.918 stack, NOT the current 0.947 one)", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Note this also explains why the public 0.918 stack's identical constants leave the whole public field at divJ~0: the entire lineage inherited the same mis-set gate.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 577, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The public 0.918 stack carries IDENTICAL constants, which is why the entire public field sits at divJ ~ 0. The whole lineage inherited the same mis-set gate."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 472, "key": "separating_features", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "| `cos_angle` | [-0.99, -0.51] | <= -0.51 | **63.7 %** |", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "cos_angle is the only feature with real one-sided power: it kills 63.7% of FP forks while retaining all 5 TPs. True divisions sit at cos -0.71..-0.76 (~135-140 deg); FP forks at -0.33. True sisters keep diverging (9.5um by t+2); FP forks stay at 5.3um. No temporal or depth gating opportunity exists - both are uniform in t and z."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 473, "key": "order_of_operations", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "**Widen first, filter second** - this is the correct order given the quadratic FP cost structure.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "WIDEN FIRST, FILTER SECOND. A precision filter on today's forks caps at +0.0027 perfect / +0.0007 honest. Widening is nearly free at this operating point: FPs going 613 -> 1200 costs only -0.0003, because the quadratic FP cost only bites once precision is already high."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 474, "key": "honest_fitting_protocol", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Fit on 44b6's 26 divisions, evaluate on 6bba's 125, and separately the reverse; report both directions and take the min.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "With 26 divisions in 44b6 and 125 in 6bba, never fit on pooled events and report pooled. Fit on 44b6's 26, evaluate on 6bba's 125, then the reverse, report both directions and take the min."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 475, "key": "d1_falsifier", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "**Kill unless `fork_at_matched_mother` rises from 0 to >= 25 across the 89 metric-reachable divisions**", "review_after": null, "source_id": 48, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 489, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "D1 kill condition, preregistered: replay both LOEO folds with the re-gated proposer and KILL unless fork_at_matched_mother rises from 0 to >=25 across the 89 metric-reachable divisions. If forks land at true mothers but divJ does not rise, the fault has moved to _is_strongly_connected_division (division_metrics.py:227-271)."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 476, "key": "the_validation_crisis", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the deployed pipeline contains a model trained on all 199 labelled crops, so the deployed system cannot be validly measured on any labelled data we hold", "review_after": null, "source_id": 49, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "validation", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE ROOT CAUSE of offline-vs-LB divergence: the deployed pipeline contained a model trained on ALL 199 labelled crops, so the deployed system could not be validly measured on any labelled data held. A lever measured +0.0144/+0.0090 on paired LOEO and +0.000 on the leaderboard. All three pre-specified explanations (weights redundancy, crop population, pooling/rounding) were REFUTED."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 477, "key": "rebuild_rule", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "That, not arm B, is the finding that gates H1.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 49, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "validation", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "RULE FOR THE REBUILD: never let any component of the deployed chain train on data you need to validate the chain on. Keep at least one embryo fully unseen by every component, or the offline instrument is structurally broken and no amount of rigour repairs it."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 478, "key": "objective_reduced", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Because `J_i . w_i == TP_i`, this collapses exactly to adj_edge_jaccard = S_i (TP_i . m_i) / S_i w_i", "review_after": null, "source_id": 50, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The objective collapses exactly: adj_edge_jaccard = SUM_i (TP_i * m_i) / SUM_i w_i, where w_i = TP_i+FP_i+FN_i and m_i = max(0, 1 - 0.1*(N_i-E_i)/E_i). It is a micro-averaged Jaccard whose numerator is per-crop multiplier-weighted. division_jaccard is micro-pooled across crops."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 479, "key": "threshold_lever_dead", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "6bba's threshold-limited miss class is 0.1% of GT (10 of 9,604)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 51, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The detection-threshold lever is DEAD on 6bba: only 0.1% of GT (10 of 9,604) is threshold-limited. Dropping tau from 0.96875 to 0.01 buys +0.10pp of GT reach for +167% nodes - catastrophic under the node-count multiplier."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 480, "key": "domain_shift_falsified", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the deployed detector scores *worse* on the family it trained on (6bba, node recall 0.8637) than on the family it has never seen (44b6, 0.8888)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 51, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "'Domain shift' is FALSIFIED as the mechanism for the 6bba deficit: the deployed detector scored WORSE on the family it trained on (6bba, node recall 0.8637) than on the family it had never seen (44b6, 0.8888). The true LOEO-strict detection gap between families is 2.5pp, not the headline 11.8pp - the headline was inflated by an all-199-train secondary detector."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 481, "key": "colab_measured_burn_rate", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "session: 8.2 units, 6.0 h, ['smoke', 'notebook']", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": 52, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED on this account 2026-08-26, better than any published rate: four Colab sessions each ran 6.0 h and consumed 8.2 / 8.4 / 9.85 / 9.9 units - about 1.37-1.65 units/hour. That is T4-class consumption. ~1000 units is therefore roughly 600-700 h of T4, NOT the A100 figure; A100 burn must be measured separately before planning around it."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 482, "key": "colab_real_risk_is_parity", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "attempt 5: Python 3.12 kernel, KGAT auth, input_root rewrite ... \"input_rewrites\": 36", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": 52, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The prior Colab attempt failed on ENVIRONMENT PARITY, not compute. Five consecutive p21-parity jobs failed across ~36 units and 4 sessions, fighting a Python 3.12 kernel, Kaggle auth, and 36 input-path rewrites to emulate /kaggle/input. Only 1 job of 6 ever completed. Budget the parity work, not the GPU hours."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 483, "key": "colab_cli_supersedes_relay", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "colab run [--gpu GPU] ... Run a local script on a fresh VM, forwarding arguments, then release it", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": 52, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "googlecolab/google-colab-cli (Apache-2.0, official Google org, v0.6.0) replaces the hand-rolled git-relay entirely: colab new --gpu A100 / colab run script.py / colab download / colab stop, plus a keep-alive daemon. Installed to ~/.local/bin/colab via a venv (Arch blocks pip per PEP 668). It does NOT expose compute-unit accounting - `colab pay` only opens the billing page - so the relay's per-job unit tracking has no CLI equivalent."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 484, "key": "codex_is_a_worker", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "[projects.\"/home/aryaarun/Work\"] trust_level = \"trusted\"", "review_after": null, "source_id": 53, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "tooling", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Codex (codex-cli 0.153.4, gpt-6-astra) is a second agent on this project. ~/Work is trusted in its config. It reads AGENTS.md, which is now the single contract - CLAUDE.md is a 4-line pointer so the two cannot drift. Ponytail 4.9.0 installed for Codex too. Given the read-only `recall` skill; `research` and `verify` withheld because they WRITE to the Claude memory store."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "id": 485, "key": "colab_cost_gate", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "failed p21_colab_parity_f0-20260826t2204 (1.44 units) ... attempt 5: Python 3.12 kernel, KGAT auth, input_root rewrite", "review_after": null, "source_id": 52, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "tooling", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Paid Colab GPU runs go through tools/colab_guard.sh, which refuses to launch without two receipts: T0/T1 local preflight and T2 Colab-CPU parity. Receipts are bound to the script's sha256 (so passing one file cannot authorise another) and expire after 6h. Evidence-driven: the old relay burned ~36 units across 4 sessions with 5 of 6 jobs failing on ENVIRONMENT PARITY, not compute - T2 is the tier that would have caught every one of them for free."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 486, "key": "ponytail_hooks_audited", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "grep for http/fetch/child_process/spawn across hooks/*.js returned only local require() of sibling modules", "review_after": null, "source_id": 52, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "tooling", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Ponytail's three Codex lifecycle hooks (SessionStart, SubagentStart, UserPromptSubmit) were read before trusting: they require only fs/path/os, make no network call, spawn no process, and write one mode flag into the plugin's own state dir. No credential or repo access."}
