{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 511, "key": "pub947/86f995b7: Edge loss is a softmax over the SOURCE axis plus focal-modulated BCE with gamma=2; dim=0 is deliberate so divisions are ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "    probs = torch.softmax(logits, dim=0)  # dim=0 intentional: divisions allowed, merges aren't\n    bce = F.binary_cross_entropy(probs, target, reduction=\"none\")\n    p_t = probs * target + (1 - probs) * (1 - target)\n    loss = ((1 - p_t) ** 2) * bce", "review_after": null, "source_id": 68, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "public-stack", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Edge loss is a softmax over the SOURCE axis plus focal-modulated BCE with gamma=2; dim=0 is deliberate so divisions are allowed but merges are not."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 512, "key": "pub947/f293afcd: Detections are extracted by max-pool local-maximum NMS followed by a sigmoid threshold - there is no top-k or proposal b", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "    pad = tuple(k // 2 for k in pool_kernel)\n    pooled = F.max_pool3d(logits, pool_kernel, stride=1, padding=pad)\n    is_peak = (logits == pooled) & (torch.sigmoid(logits) > det_threshold)\n    peak_idx = torch.nonzero(is_peak[0, 0])  # (N, 3)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 68, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "public-stack", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Detections are extracted by max-pool local-maximum NMS followed by a sigmoid threshold - there is no top-k or proposal budget, every qualifying local max is kept."}
