{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 589, "key": "hack/3f685c7c: MECHANISM (edges): a predicted edge is only eligible to be a false positive if one of its endpoints matched a GT node, s", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "edge_attrs = edge_attrs.with_columns(\n        (pl.col(\"out_valid\") | pl.col(\"in_valid\")).alias(\"pred_valid\"),\n    )\n...\n        edge_valid_pred = int(edge_attrs[\"pred_valid\"].sum())\n        edge_fp = edge_valid_pred - edge_tp", "review_after": null, "source_id": 69, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric-exploit", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MECHANISM (edges): a predicted edge is only eligible to be a false positive if one of its endpoints matched a GT node, so edges between out-of-volume fake nodes cost nothing in the edge Jaccard."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 590, "key": "hack/2cd2454c: MECHANISM (divisions): division candidates are taken from `visited`, the full set of graph nodes reachable from a matche", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "for matched_subset, visited in components:\n            comp_attrs = matched_attrs.filter(...)\n            if _has_stage_coverage(comp_attrs, gt_div, div_node):\n                div_candidates |= visited & pred_div_nodes\n        candidates[div_node] = div_candidates", "review_after": null, "source_id": 69, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric-exploit", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MECHANISM (divisions): division candidates are taken from `visited`, the full set of graph nodes reachable from a matched component, so making the whole prediction one weakly-connected component via the hub exposes every predicted dividing node to every GT division."}
