{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 610, "key": "mechanism", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "div_candidates |= visited & pred_div_nodes ... fp = max(0, matched_pred_divs - tp)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 69, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric-exploit", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Hub node at t=-1000, (z,y,x)=(-10000,-10000,-10000), wired to every real track root, plus synthetic forks at t=-999,-997,... It works on two host-code facts: score_divisions draws candidates from `visited` (everything reachable in a matched component), so one hub makes the whole prediction one weakly-connected component and every dividing node becomes a candidate; and division FPs are counted only for forks that MATCHED a GT node, which a fork at -10000um never does. TP with zero FP, division_jaccard -> ~1.0, worth the full +0.1."}
