{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 635, "key": "div/2133d7dd: Two competitors on the same 0.948 LB can need opposite work: div_j 0.30 requires edge 0.918, div_j 0.15 requir", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "if your division_jaccard is 0.30, you only need adj_edge_jaccard 0.918 if it is 0.15, you need adj_edge_jaccard 0.933 Those two people should be working on opposite things, and the leaderboard shows them the same number.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 72, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Two competitors on the same 0.948 LB can need opposite work: div_j 0.30 requires edge 0.918, div_j 0.15 requires edge 0.933, and the leaderboard hides which."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 636, "key": "div/7fa2ee96: The 0.22 paired-LB estimate is confounded: dropping a division also drops a daughter edge, so the 0.022 delta ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "if turning off division creation means your linker only keeps one of the two daughter links instead of two, the dropped daughter becomes an edge false negative, not just a division miss. That would pull edge_jaccard down as well", "review_after": null, "source_id": 72, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The 0.22 paired-LB estimate is confounded: dropping a division also drops a daughter edge, so the 0.022 delta splits between the edge and division terms and 0.22 is a bound, not a measurement."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 637, "key": "div/939aee53: A nearest-parent candidate graph at R~9.9um K<=10 covers only ~88% of the 151 GT division forks versus ~99.7% ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "a simple nearest-parent candidate graph (R≈9.9µm, K≤10) only reaches ~88% coverage on the 151 GT division forks, versus ~99.7% on plain continuation edges — so there's a real, measurable gap concentrated on divisions before any classifier even gets involved", "review_after": null, "source_id": 72, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A nearest-parent candidate graph at R~9.9um K<=10 covers only ~88% of the 151 GT division forks versus ~99.7% of continuation edges, a hard ceiling on division_jaccard before any classifier runs."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 638, "key": "div/1ee99dd3: One competitor's ILP never exceeded division_jaccard 0.0004 at any division weight; at weight 0.5 it found div", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "For me division_jaccard never rises above 0.0004, at any weight tested. Even at 0.5, where the ILP does find 1 real division (div_tp=1), it does so alongside 3260 false ones. div_j = tp/(tp+fp+fn) ≈ 1/3260 - swamped to near-zero by the FP volume.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 72, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "One competitor's ILP never exceeded division_jaccard 0.0004 at any division weight; at weight 0.5 it found div_tp=1 alongside 3260 false forks, so weight-tuning alone cannot produce a positive division score."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 639, "key": "div/f81d4565: A Hungarian 1:1 linker with divisions bolted on afterwards as a hand-written distance+image rule reaches divJ ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "my linker is basically 1:1 right now. hungarian assignment frame to frame. then i add divisions in a totally separate step after on top of the result. so the division decision never actually sees the model. its js a hand written rule with distance and image checks. my divJ is around 0.12", "review_after": null, "source_id": 72, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A Hungarian 1:1 linker with divisions bolted on afterwards as a hand-written distance+image rule reaches divJ ~0.12."}
