{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 729, "key": "data/25dcf054: All synthetic division supervision lives in 6-frame 64x64x64 already-pooled crops; the 1,539 native-resolution", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "`static/vol_XXXXX.npz` ... | `volume` | `(64, 256, 256)` uint16 | native-resolution intensity | | `centroids` | `(N, 3)` float32 | ... `sequences/seq_XXXX.npz` ... | `volumes` | `(T, 64, 64, 64)` uint16 | already pooled (stride 4x), the resolution a detector sees |", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "All synthetic division supervision lives in 6-frame 64x64x64 already-pooled crops; the 1,539 native-resolution 256x256 static volumes carry centroids only and NO lineage graph at all."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 730, "key": "data/3aa3c9ae: The 165,267 figure counts mitotic PARENT nodes (fork events), equivalent to 330,534 daughter nodes or 330,534 ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A \"division\" in the 165,267 figure is a mitotic parent — one fork event. Not a daughter, and not a parent->daughter edge. ... 165,267 mitotic parents (fork events) is the published figure. That corresponds to 330,534 daughter nodes, and 330,534 parent->daughter division edges, out of 4,056,226 to...", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The 165,267 figure counts mitotic PARENT nodes (fork events), equivalent to 330,534 daughter nodes or 330,534 parent->daughter edges, out of 4,056,226 total nodes."}
