{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 733, "key": "data/e07c9998: The synthetic division rate is deliberately inflated roughly 15.7x over the real rate, so any loss trained on ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The division rate is deliberately inflated (4.07% of nodes vs ~0.26% in reality). A model starved of examples never learns mitosis. Re-weight your loss by the real rate if you need calibrated priors.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The synthetic division rate is deliberately inflated roughly 15.7x over the real rate, so any loss trained on it needs reweighting before its priors are calibrated."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 734, "key": "data/ad2b3483: The author concedes the synthetic data's weakest axes are exactly nucleus texture and contrast, i.e. the appea", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Distribution match is partial. Nucleus texture and contrast are the weakest axes. The value here is the labels — density, lineage and mitosis — much more than photorealism.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The author concedes the synthetic data's weakest axes are exactly nucleus texture and contrast, i.e. the appearance channel a detector trains on."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 735, "key": "data/98dd1034: A subtle synthetic-data trap: both daughters inherit the parent's track_id, so nodes[:,4] is a lineage/clone i", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "both daughters inherit the parent's track_id. So nodes[:, 4] is a lineage/clone id, not a unique track — after a division, two distinct tracks share it. ... If you build your candidate graph off track_id expecting uniqueness, it will look like cells teleport.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A subtle synthetic-data trap: both daughters inherit the parent's track_id, so nodes[:,4] is a lineage/clone id and is NOT unique per track after a division."}
