{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 740, "key": "data/00389f3c: Zebrahub volumes are OME-Zarr v2 (.zattrs, 5D TCZYX) while the competition uses Zarr v3 (zarr.json, 4D TZYX) -", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "=== OME zarr root meta ZSNS001 === (.zattrs served)  ...  zarr.json:404", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Zebrahub volumes are OME-Zarr v2 (.zattrs, 5D TCZYX) while the competition uses Zarr v3 (zarr.json, 4D TZYX) - a loader written for one will not open the other."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 741, "key": "data/a4ad1851: Zebrahub's *_tracks.csv lineages are Ultrack-generated pseudo-labels, not manually curated, carrying Ultrack's", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The tracks are algorithm-generated, not manually curated. The *_tracks.csv lineages were produced with Ultrack (Bragantini et al., Royer Lab / CZ Biohub, Nature Methods 2025), an automated segmentation + linking pipeline. They're high quality, but they're effectively pseudo-labels", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Zebrahub's *_tracks.csv lineages are Ultrack-generated pseudo-labels, not manually curated, carrying Ultrack's own error modes around divisions and dense regions."}
