{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 751, "key": "data/08b1c8f9: THE SINGLE MOST DANGEROUS DEFECT: in 6bba_fc516dc6 the volumes at t=81 and t=82 are byte-identical yet the GT ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "np.array_equal(volume[81], volume[82]) is True , and the subtraction contains zero nonzero voxels. The GT edge is: 82001039 : (t,z,y,x) = (81,23,175,169) 83001053 : (t,z,y,x) = (82,18,179,161) With voxel scale (1.625, 0.40625, 0.40625) um, this is an 8.90 um displacement.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE SINGLE MOST DANGEROUS DEFECT: in 6bba_fc516dc6 the volumes at t=81 and t=82 are byte-identical yet the GT edge moves 8.90 um - larger than the 7 um matching radius - so copying a detection across a frozen frame is guaranteed to miss."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 752, "key": "data/9c4fd324: The 8.90 um frozen-frame jump is almost entirely in Z (23->18 voxels = 8.125 um of the 8.90), i.e. it is an an", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "show_crops(22, 81, 24) vs show_crops(22, 82, 24): XY panels and the red centroid are visually unchanged; only the XZ/YZ red dot shifts. plt.scatter(169,175); plt.scatter(161,179); plt.imshow(img[82,18]) shows BOTH points on one elongated blob.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The 8.90 um frozen-frame jump is almost entirely in Z (23->18 voxels = 8.125 um of the 8.90), i.e. it is an annotation wobble along the 4x-anisotropic axis on one elongated nucleus, not real motion."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 753, "key": "data/004c4cc8: The frozen-frame GT wobble is not a one-off: only one cell in that frame moved, and the cell is elongated with", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I checked the other cells in 82nd frame, all have the same values as 81st except this one. This is actually a large cell, it's Z span itself is >15 voxels. If testset has such cells then even if our model predicts the right center it won't be able to cover both within 7um.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The frozen-frame GT wobble is not a one-off: only one cell in that frame moved, and the cell is elongated with a Z-span over 15 voxels, so even a perfectly centred prediction cannot cover both annotations within 7 um."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 754, "key": "data/bac77347: GT tracks contain outright wrong edges detectable by neighbour-motion consistency, e.g. 6bba_1d0d8384 track_id", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Not all edge annotations are correct. But the error rate is very low. Here is an error detected by checking neighbouring cell motion", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GT tracks contain outright wrong edges detectable by neighbour-motion consistency, e.g. 6bba_1d0d8384 track_id 73 spikes at frame 16 onto the wrong nucleus."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 755, "key": "data/73a1b414: BOUNDARY-CELL FRAGMENTATION: in 44b6_12dfb391 one cell is annotated as two separate GT lineages (t=21-24 and t", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Track A: t=21 to t=24 (4 nodes), ending at x=139, y=0, z=80 Track B: t=29 to t=37 (9 nodes), starting at x=143, y=0, z=80 The spatial distance between the end of Track A and the start of Track B is only 4.0 um , with identical y=0 and z=80 coordinates.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "BOUNDARY-CELL FRAGMENTATION: in 44b6_12dfb391 one cell is annotated as two separate GT lineages (t=21-24 and t=29-37) 4.0 um apart at y=0, penalising any tracker that correctly links across the field-of-view edge."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 756, "key": "data/f5c6ead2: A competitor who hand-checked GT against his own visual tracking reports disagreeing with the GT in the great ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I find that I agree with my algorithms 95% of the time, and GT only 5% of the time in these cases, and I have seen quite a few of them. In some cases GT does not seem to see that the cell has split, or that the cell has moved slightly", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A competitor who hand-checked GT against his own visual tracking reports disagreeing with the GT in the great majority of disputed cases."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 757, "key": "data/4f593db0: Independent physical evidence of mislabelled divisions: post-split daughter volume in the GT averages ~0.75 of", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "each cells volume after a split should be 0.5 of the volume of the parent before the split. However, in GT this is not the case. On average, volume after split in GT is closer to 0.75. ... I labelled my own dataset and measure this same measurement at 0.5.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Independent physical evidence of mislabelled divisions: post-split daughter volume in the GT averages ~0.75 of the parent instead of the expected 0.5, while the same measurement on hand-labelled data gives 0.5."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 758, "key": "data/1c03594b: Some annotated nodes are invisible in the image: node 53000565 at slice 31 of frame 52 in 6bba_3a1849c2 sits o", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I am looking at the track for node 53000565 . This node is specifically at slice 31 of frame 52 of the video 6bba_3a1849c2 and is supposed to be at the red dot in the following picture", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Some annotated nodes are invisible in the image: node 53000565 at slice 31 of frame 52 in 6bba_3a1849c2 sits on flat background with the nearest visible nucleus tens of pixels away."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 759, "key": "data/38158ed4: The leading explanation for invisible annotated nodes is temporal interpolation of the annotation, i.e. a node", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "It can be false positive or results of interpolation. Eg annotation label frame t=1 and t=3 and interpolate for t=2", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The leading explanation for invisible annotated nodes is temporal interpolation of the annotation, i.e. a node asserted at t=2 from labels at t=1 and t=3 rather than observed."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 760, "key": "data/b91db8eb: GT tracks also contain long-range spatial jumps visible as straight cross-volume edges when the lineage is plo", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "At first, i thought not all ground truths are correct. Then, on inspection, i find the following are quite common 1) some frames are frozen. i.e subraction of vol at t and t+1 gives exactly zero 2) there are suddent jumps in time (global movement of whole volume)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GT tracks also contain long-range spatial jumps visible as straight cross-volume edges when the lineage is plotted in 3D (example: 6bba_f20478e9, 40 tracks, four such edges circled)."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 761, "key": "data/538249ec: Upstream reference point for GT quality: the Ultrack paper's own figure reports a median error-free track leng", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "panel d: 'proportion of error-free tracks' vs 'error-free tracks length (frames)', curves for fish 1/2/3 and mean, dashed guide lines at y=0.50 meeting x=62", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Upstream reference point for GT quality: the Ultrack paper's own figure reports a median error-free track length of about 62 frames across three fish, i.e. half of all tracks break before 62 frames even in the tool that produced these labels."}
