{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 764, "key": "data/8f83a58d: The synthetic dataset's author independently concedes the same bias: annotators label unambiguous cells, so an", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the 0.91-0.94 real reference comes from the sparse annotations (~2.8% of nuclei), and annotators tend to label unambiguous cells - so that reference is probably optimistic, and I haven't measured how real recall varies with density.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The synthetic dataset's author independently concedes the same bias: annotators label unambiguous cells, so any recall measured against the sparse annotations is optimistic."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 765, "key": "data/e56506ea: Counter-evidence that the bias is not toward brightness alone: at least one annotated node sits on visually fl", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I was looking though my false negatives and realised that some of the nodes cannot be seen properly and i was wondering whether thsoe where annotation artifacts or cells can actually be this dim.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Counter-evidence that the bias is not toward brightness alone: at least one annotated node sits on visually flat background, so a brightness prior fitted to annotated cells will not explain the full label set."}
