{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 770, "key": "data/69fa929d: A competitor probing the test set concluded it is materially smaller than train (~2/3 or less), which contradi", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I probed the test set and found that its size is significantly smaller than the training set. Of course, it's also possible that the embryonic cell development nodes in the test set are simpler. Assuming the development process is the same, the size is roughly only 2/3 or even less.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 73, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A competitor probing the test set concluded it is materially smaller than train (~2/3 or less), which contradicts the host's 'roughly similar in size' and the data description - treat test size as uncertain."}
