{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 822, "key": "meth/18a1cbfd: Local post-processing gains frequently do not transfer: one participant reports post-processing pushes local s", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I have tried pilkwang model family (3d Unet) so far, without further fine tuning but it seem to be stuck at a certain score.\nI have tried a lot of post processing techniques, it does push score locally but LD score drops.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Local post-processing gains frequently do not transfer: one participant reports post-processing pushes local score up while the leaderboard score drops."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 823, "key": "meth/2d3801d4: Another participant tuning post-processing on the public checkpoint went 0.907 to 0.916 and could not reach 0.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Im stuck with public data starting @ .907 with tuned upto .916 but cant make it cross nor touch .92\nTried multiple algos but score remains the same. \nNot in the position to train my own model from scratch.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Another participant tuning post-processing on the public checkpoint went 0.907 to 0.916 and could not reach 0.92, corroborating the post-processing ceiling."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 824, "key": "meth/136b5649: The detector's junk candidate pool, not the linker, is diagnosed as the bottleneck: the detector finds the rea", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the detector is finding the real cells, but it is also producing an enormous junk candidate pool. The linker then has to choose among those candidates which ends up with wrong linking", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The detector's junk candidate pool, not the linker, is diagnosed as the bottleneck: the detector finds the real cells but also emits an enormous junk pool the linker must choose among."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 825, "key": "meth/b94f7f43: The GNN case is weak on graph structure alone: the ground truth is 4,435 disjoint trees of which at most 151 b", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The GT is 4,435 disjoint trees, and at most 151 of them branch. So ≥96.6% are pure linear chains", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The GNN case is weak on graph structure alone: the ground truth is 4,435 disjoint trees of which at most 151 branch, so at least 96.6% of tracks are pure linear chains."}
