{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 829, "key": "meth/460f4b6e: Training a TemporalUNet3D on Kaggle's sparse annotation is reported unstable: both train and validation loss t", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "So both validation and train loss took a U turn upwards half the way, why is this happening? Any tips to stablise training on sparse annotations?\n\nWhat kind of loss function should be used?", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Training a TemporalUNet3D on Kaggle's sparse annotation is reported unstable: both train and validation loss turn upwards partway through training."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 830, "key": "meth/592e62b2: A recommended sequencing: learn tracks with no division first (single birth and death), then handle division a", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "my suggestion is to learn track without cell division first (i.e. all tracks has only one BIRTH and DEATH). cell dvision is then handled at post-processing or stage 2 (e.g. classifier to decide if there is a split based on appearance changes and longer track cues).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A recommended sequencing: learn tracks with no division first (single birth and death), then handle division at post-processing or a stage-2 classifier using appearance change and longer track cues."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 831, "key": "meth/18df130e: Ultrack is characterised as multiple-hypothesis tracking over divided cells; if the GT came from Ultrack, the ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Assume the GT is from Ultrack, then i should reverse engineer. If I were to convert ultrack to a deep net, my link transformer should have been: 1) no division head softmax (one Nt, all other Nt+1) 2) division head softmax (one Nt, all other choose(Nt+1,2) )", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Ultrack is characterised as multiple-hypothesis tracking over divided cells; if the GT came from Ultrack, the implied linker is two softmax heads - no-division over N_{t+1}, division over choose(N_{t+1},2) - plus two node-detector instance heads."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 832, "key": "meth/6361126e: An ILP-as-label-propagator recipe: overwrite dense linker edge scores with hard sparse-GT constraints (+2 corr", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "train link predictor and make link probability. Then add modify the link probability so that if it is hit prob is 2. If it is fp, it is -2. Miss is 4. The run ipl. Verify the results have 100% jaccrad. All dense link are use for training the next refinement", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "An ILP-as-label-propagator recipe: overwrite dense linker edge scores with hard sparse-GT constraints (+2 correct, -2 contradicts, +4 required-but-missing), solve the ILP, keep the graph only if its Jaccard against the sparse annotation is 1.0, then train a refinement linker on the dense edges it selected."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 833, "key": "meth/2c8bdd33: That ILP-pseudo-label recipe carries an explicit caveat: 100% agreement with the sparse GT does not prove the ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "100% sparse Jaccard does not prove the unannotated dense edges are correct. Many dense graphs can potentially agree perfectly with the sparse GT. So I would not blindly train on every ILP-selected edge with equal weight.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "That ILP-pseudo-label recipe carries an explicit caveat: 100% agreement with the sparse GT does not prove the unannotated dense edges are correct, so they should not be trained on with equal weight."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 834, "key": "meth/dac8ea2b: A late reframing from the FOCUS-3D author: because labels are partial and ambiguous, the right formulation is ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "There are ambiguities and there is inly partial labels. Instead of learning perfect predictors, the focus should generate hypothesis and test.eg different way to link up assume with and without division and score hypothesis", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A late reframing from the FOCUS-3D author: because labels are partial and ambiguous, the right formulation is hypothesis generation and testing rather than learning a perfect predictor."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 835, "key": "meth/8366552f: Speculation worth testing: the competition ground truth is suspected to have been produced by an open-source 3", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Further, i think gt annotation must have used some open source cell instance detector. I suspect it it cellpose3d or stardist3d with manual collection.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Speculation worth testing: the competition ground truth is suspected to have been produced by an open-source 3D instance detector, specifically cellpose3d or stardist3d, with manual correction."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 836, "key": "meth/2289dca4: A suggested subpixel refinement: nudge the Kaggle GT to gt+dzyx within the 7 um error limit to improve link pr", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Let gt be the Kaggle annotation; you can refine ground truth to gt+dzxy so that it is still within the 7um error limit but drastically improves link probability. Also coord could be subpixel and use F.graid sample to sample feature.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A suggested subpixel refinement: nudge the Kaggle GT to gt+dzyx within the 7 um error limit to improve link probability, and sample features at subpixel coords via grid_sample - flagged by its own author as overfitting-prone."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 837, "key": "meth/bcc422b5: Candidate counts make all-pairs attention cheap: ~800 candidates per volume gives 640k pair relations per fram", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "each volume now has about 800 cell candiates, this makes pairing or multi link trasnformer attnetion space small [...] per-frame self attention: 5 x 800^2 = 3.2M / cross-frame attention: t <-> t+1 only 4 x 800^2 = 2.56M", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Candidate counts make all-pairs attention cheap: ~800 candidates per volume gives 640k pair relations per frame, and a 5-frame window needs only ~6M interactions with per-frame self-attention plus t<->t+1 cross-attention."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 838, "key": "meth/62cb2458: SCORER: adjusted = max(0, jaccard * (1 - 0.1*(N_pred-N_true)/N_true)) with N_true from estimated_number_of_nod", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "adjusted = max(0, jaccard * (1 - 0.1 * (N_pred - N_true) / N_true))\n\nwith N_true read from estimated_number_of_nodes in the ground truth metadata. [...] Scoring above 1.0 is not a bug and the evaluation page says as much. Treat 1.0 as a reference point, not a ceiling.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "SCORER: adjusted = max(0, jaccard * (1 - 0.1*(N_pred-N_true)/N_true)) with N_true from estimated_number_of_nodes; because GT is sparsely labelled a faithful prediction scores ABOVE 1.0."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 839, "key": "meth/08790025: HOST STATEMENT: perfectly duplicated edges are filtered before scoring the edge Jaccard and each GT edge can s", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "perfectly duplicated edges are filtered out before scoring the edge Jaccard, this might be why you are not seeing a change in the Jaccard score, each ground truth edge can only used for a single TP. [...] This should not allow you to hack (i.e. increase) your score.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "HOST STATEMENT: perfectly duplicated edges are filtered before scoring the edge Jaccard and each GT edge can serve only one TP, so track duplication does not game the metric."}
