{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 866, "key": "meth/fe6eeb64: The support pack fixes a real flip-augmentation bug present in the reference baseline: the baseline's combined", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "-            coords[masks, dim] = shape[dim] - coords[masks, dim] - 1\n+            dim_coords = coords[..., dim]\n+            dim_coords[masks] = shape[dim] - dim_coords[masks] - 1\n+            coords[..., dim] = dim_coords", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The support pack fixes a real flip-augmentation bug present in the reference baseline: the baseline's combined boolean-plus-integer index assignment on coords is replaced with an explicit per-axis read-modify-write."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 867, "key": "meth/5360b3ac: The linker's positional input is a relative coordinate difference scaled by 1/100 concatenated onto the two no", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "rel = (cc.unsqueeze(2) - cc1.unsqueeze(1)) / 100.0\n                return _pm(torch.cat([qe, ke, rel], dim=-1)).squeeze(-1)\n[train] _POS_EMBED_DIM = 8   # per axis; total = 4 axes × _POS_EMBED_DIM = 32", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The linker's positional input is a relative coordinate difference scaled by 1/100 concatenated onto the two node embeddings in the pair MLP, and node features are 32 UNet channels plus a 32-dim sinusoidal 4-axis (t,z,y,x) positional embedding."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 868, "key": "meth/095dc8ef: False-positive detections ARE supervised during training: build_matched_edge_targets zeroes every edge touchin", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "valid_t = mt >= 0\n        valid_t1 = mt1 >= 0\n        valid_mask = valid_t.unsqueeze(1) & valid_t1.unsqueeze(0)\n        block = gt_trans[safe_t][:, safe_t1] * valid_mask.float()", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "False-positive detections ARE supervised during training: build_matched_edge_targets zeroes every edge touching an unmatched detection, so an unmatched peak is taught to link to nothing - meaning detector precision is already implicitly in the linker's loss."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 869, "key": "meth/3059480e: The reference training defaults ARE the public pipeline's settings - lr 1e-3, batch_size 16, downsample (1,4,4", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "    lr: float = 1e-3,\n    batch_size: int = 16,\n    downsample: tuple[int, ...] = (1, 4, 4),\n    det_neg_weight: float = 1e-2,\n    pool_kernel_um: float = 5.0,", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The reference training defaults ARE the public pipeline's settings - lr 1e-3, batch_size 16, downsample (1,4,4), det_neg_weight 1e-2, pool_kernel_um 5.0 - so the 0.947 tier is the organisers' untuned defaults run for 400 epochs."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 870, "key": "meth/5ae9d9f4: MEASURED CORRECTION: the (1,4,4) downsample does NOT destroy annotated ground-truth nodes - across 30 local tr", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "files=30 total_gt_nodes=7584 collapsed=0 rate=0.00000", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED CORRECTION: the (1,4,4) downsample does NOT destroy annotated ground-truth nodes - across 30 local train geffs and 7,584 sparse GT nodes, exactly ZERO collapsed to a duplicate (t,z,y//4,x//4) voxel, so the code's collapse warning never fires on the sparse annotation."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 871, "key": "meth/4b64f4f9: MEASURED: every single ground-truth edge in the 31 local train geffs spans exactly one frame - there are NO sk", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "files=31 nodes=8154 edges=7998 ... edge frame-gap histogram: {1: 7998}", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED: every single ground-truth edge in the 31 local train geffs spans exactly one frame - there are NO skip-frame edges in the GT at all, so gap recovery cannot mean emitting t->t+2 edges; it must mean recovering the missing intermediate NODE and then two 1-frame edges."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 872, "key": "meth/074adcfc: MEASURED: divisions are extraordinarily sparse in the supervision - only 9 nodes out of 8,154 have out-degree ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "divisions(outdeg>=2)=9 (0.1125% of edges)\nout-degree histogram: {1: 7980, 2: 9}", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED: divisions are extraordinarily sparse in the supervision - only 9 nodes out of 8,154 have out-degree 2 across 31 local train geffs, 0.11% of the 7,998 edges, and no node ever has out-degree 3 or more."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 873, "key": "meth/eea0e67b: MEASURED: ground-truth node coordinates are stored as int64 voxel indices, not floats - there is no subpixel i", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "\"shape\": [52], \"data_type\": \"int64\", ... \"codecs\": [{\"name\": \"bytes\", \"configuration\": {\"endian\": \"little\"}}, {\"name\": \"zstd\", ...}]", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED: ground-truth node coordinates are stored as int64 voxel indices, not floats - there is no subpixel information in the annotation, which bounds how much a subpixel-refinement head can recover."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 874, "key": "meth/789fe26c: FOCUS-3D is NOT a U-Net: it is a 3D Mask2Former instance segmenter on a 3D masked-autoencoder ViT backbone (EM", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "META_ARCHITECTURE: \"MaskFormer\"\n  BACKBONE:\n    NAME: \"D2MAE3DBackbone\"\n    IMG_SIZE: [32, 96, 96]\n    PATCH_SIZE: [8,12,12]\n    IN_CHANS: 1\n    EMBED_DIM: 1008\n    DEPTH: 24", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "FOCUS-3D is NOT a U-Net: it is a 3D Mask2Former instance segmenter on a 3D masked-autoencoder ViT backbone (EMBED_DIM 1008, DEPTH 24 - ViT-L scale) with a ViT-Adapter, i.e. the foundation-model route for this task."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 875, "key": "meth/9b611f60: FOCUS-3D's head is a MSDeformAttnPixelDecoder3D with 6 encoder layers feeding a 9-layer multi-scale masked tra", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "NAME: \"MSDeformAttnPixelDecoder3D\"\n    TRANSFORMER_ENC_LAYERS: 6\n[MASK_FORMER] NUM_OBJECT_QUERIES: 300\n    DEC_LAYERS: 9\n    DN : \"seg\"\n    DN_NUM : 100", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "FOCUS-3D's head is a MSDeformAttnPixelDecoder3D with 6 encoder layers feeding a 9-layer multi-scale masked transformer decoder with 300 object queries and segmentation denoising (DN_NUM 100) - enormously heavier than a 1x1x1 detection head, which is why it times out as an in-notebook detector."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 876, "key": "meth/6a894155: FOCUS-3D ships TWO domain checkpoints - Nuclei and Membrane - and the competition data is the Nuclei case; the", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "CHECKPOINTS = {\n    \"Nuclei\": MODEL_VOLUME / \"model_final_nuclei.pth\",\n    \"Membrane\": MODEL_VOLUME / \"model_final_membrane.pth\",\n}\n[README] The Space uses the pure-PyTorch `inference_win` runtime copied from the FOCUS-3D project ... does not require Detectron2.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "FOCUS-3D ships TWO domain checkpoints - Nuclei and Membrane - and the competition data is the Nuclei case; the Space runs a pure-PyTorch inference path that needs no Detectron2, so it is usable offline without the full research stack."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 877, "key": "meth/62660d64: FOCUS-3D's demo takes explicit anisotropy and scale hyperparameters - Z resolution (ratio of Z to XY resolutio", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Z resolution / Ratio of the Z-axis resolution to the XY-plane resolution. 4 | Cell radius / Estimated cell radius in the XY plane, in pixels. 15 | Background intensity 0 | Image type: Nuclei", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "FOCUS-3D's demo takes explicit anisotropy and scale hyperparameters - Z resolution (ratio of Z to XY resolution) and estimated cell radius in XY pixels - matching the competition's (1,4,4) anisotropy at Z-resolution 4 and radius ~15 px."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 878, "key": "meth/c96f7e35: CONCLUSION FOR Q7: the only publicly evidenced thing that beats a 3D U-Net heatmap detector on this data is a ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "First verify the recall error of focus3d on kaggle nodes after trying several parameters search. If you are satisfied, train link/track transformer on focus3d zyx [...] Finally train a point predictor using simple unet to distill focus3d results.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 74, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CONCLUSION FOR Q7: the only publicly evidenced thing that beats a 3D U-Net heatmap detector on this data is a ViT-L-scale MAE-pretrained 3D Mask2Former (FOCUS-3D), and it is not deployable inside the submission budget - so its value is strictly as an offline dense pseudo-label generator to distil into a small U-Net."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 879, "key": "our_best_is_0932_not_0925", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "55915569 ... publicScore 0.932 ... SubmissionStatus.COMPLETE", "review_after": null, "source_id": 75, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CORRECTION from the live submission ledger: our best public score is 0.932, achieved twice (2026-08-30 and 2026-08-31), not the 0.925 recorded in facts.yaml as FACT-0001 on 2026-08-24. The campaign continued another week after that fact was written. ~23 submissions, ALL status COMPLETE - we have never hit a scoring failure."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 880, "key": "our_own_fork_ablation_measured_it (SUPERSEDED 2026-09-11: measured directly with the patched scorer - forks give 0 TP, 9 FP, and cost 0.0041 of edge term. The +0.019 LB delta is NOT the division term.)", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "p15 fork-free diagnostic: OUTPUT_SAFE_DIVISIONS=0 on P9; returns pure adj_edge -> 0.906", "review_after": null, "source_id": 75, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 1186, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "OUR OWN MEASURED DIVISION CONTRIBUTION, from the submission ledger. p15 (55768476) ran OUTPUT_SAFE_DIVISIONS=0 on the P9 champion - 'returns pure adj_edge' - and scored 0.906. P9 with forks enabled scored 0.925. Delta +0.019. If that were purely the division term it implies divJ ~ 0.19, against today's rank 1's implied ~0.235. So our prior campaign was already NEAR the division frontier, not at ~0 like the rest of the field. CAVEAT: removing fork edges also removes edge TPs, so the delta is not purely the division term - decompose it with evaluate_datasets() locally before betting on it."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 881, "key": "THE_submission_trap_silent_zero", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "No format error was raised (the file was valid CSV, all columns correct, all datasets present), so it silently scored 0.0.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "ops", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE TRAP MOST LIKELY TO COST US A RUN. Edges spanning non-consecutive frames score an EXACT 0.0 with NO diagnostic signal. Worked case (topic 728613): two submissions scored exactly 0.0 against ~0.57 locally, because a time-budget strategy subsampled frames with a stride and produced t=0->5, t=5->10 edges. GT edges only ever connect t->t+1 and the patched scorer FILTERS non-consecutive edges out BEFORE counting, so TP is structurally zero regardless of detection quality. 'No format error was raised (the file was valid CSV, all columns correct, all datasets present), so it silently scored 0.0.' The pressure that causes this arrives in the FINAL WEEK: the rerun takes 5-12h against a hard 12h ceiling, the visible test clips run ~50x faster and tell you nothing, and the reflex when a run looks tight is to skip frames. FIX: process a CONTIGUOUS block from t=0 (that participant went 0.0 -> 0.366 -> 0.380), and gate every submission on a nonconsecutive_edges check computed from submission.csv alone."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 882, "key": "offline_installable_scorer_exists", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "14 randomised perturbation families ... 84 cases, 0 mismatches on TP/FP/FN", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A numpy+scipy reimplementation of the scorer exists that needs NO tracksdata, NO torch and NO git commit: sleepymegacat/the-metric-decides-your-architecture-8-measured, verified against the official implementation across '14 randomised perturbation families ... 84 cases, 0 mismatches on TP/FP/FN'. It is installable in the internet-disabled rerun, which the official scorer is NOT."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 883, "key": "NMS_quality_outranks_everything (SUPERSEDED 2026-09-11 by EXP-2/EXP-3: the halving claim does not reproduce - duplicates cost roughly proportionally (-2.8% at 2%, -23% at 20%). LOCALISATION outranks NMS: the 2.0->2.5um centroid step alone costs 4x what a 2% duplication rate does.)", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A single duplicate detection 0.4 um away halves the edge Jaccard (1.000 -> 0.500)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 1207, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED AND DECISIVE: a SINGLE duplicate detection 0.4um away HALVES the edge Jaccard, 1.000 -> 0.500. Centroid error has a cliff at sigma ~2um, far inside the 7um matching radius: 2.5um costs 16%, 3um costs 41%, 4um costs 74% - driven by the ~9-10um inter-cell spacing, not by cell size. NMS quality and localisation accuracy outrank every other lever available."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 884, "key": "docs_contradict_code_on_gap_edges", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Drop edges that do not connect consecutive frames ... This removes backward-in-time edges", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The official metrics.md AND the organisers' own test docstring both say a non-consecutive-frame edge counts as a FALSE POSITIVE. The live code DROPS it instead - 'Drop edges that do not connect consecutive frames'. The code wins. This filter is ABSENT from the pre-patch scorer, so anything calibrated before 2026-07-17 scores gap edges differently from the live metric. Consequence: a gap edge scores identically to predicting nothing."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 885, "key": "per_movie_motion_gate_is_untaken", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the public 0.908 pipelines inherit the metric's 7 um node-matching tolerance as their motion gate", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "UNTAKEN IDEA: the public 0.908 pipelines inherit the metric's 7um NODE-MATCHING tolerance as their MOTION gate, which discards ~2% of true links for free. The loss is per-movie - a fifth of movies lose nothing, the worst loses one link in seven - so a per-movie p99 gate beats any constant."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 886, "key": "plateau_ties_break_on_earliest_submission", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "242 teams share the displayed 0.946 and 178 share 0.947", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "242 teams share the displayed 0.946 and 178 share 0.947; rank 50 = 0.948, rank 100 = 0.947. Our best is 0.932, so the gap is ~0.015 of REAL score, not a tie-break. But ties DO break on earliest submission, so a score-neutral resubmission at the plateau strictly LOSES rank."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 887, "key": "synthetic_pretraining_failed_for_its_own_author", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "all three fusions scored below plain DoG-max, 0.82/0.75/0.827 vs 0.836", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED NEGATIVE against the 18.5GB synthetic set, from the dataset's OWN AUTHOR: all three fusions scored BELOW plain DoG-max - 0.82 / 0.75 / 0.827 against 0.836. Combined with node-count tuning (zhincez: offline +0.013, LB -0.004, three datapoints), these are two levers not worth re-spending compute on."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 888, "key": "meta/7aa4f601: A submission can score EXACTLY 0.0 with no error raised if any predicted edge links non-consecutive timepoints", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Ground truth edges only ever connect strictly consecutive timepoints (t -> t+1). An edge between non-consecutive frames can never match a GT edge under the official metric, so every single edge I submitted was structurally unmatchable — TP=0 across the board", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A submission can score EXACTLY 0.0 with no error raised if any predicted edge links non-consecutive timepoints; GT edges only ever connect t->t+1, so stride/frame-skipping for speed makes every edge structurally unmatchable."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 889, "key": "meta/7d95a99e: The fix for the exact-0.0 trap is to process a CONTIGUOUS block of frames from t=0 per dataset (sized to the t", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instead of subsampling with a stride, process a contiguous block of frames from t=0 for each dataset (sized proportionally to the global time budget). This guarantees every edge connects t and t+1. Went from 0.0 -> 0.366 -> 0.380", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The fix for the exact-0.0 trap is to process a CONTIGUOUS block of frames from t=0 per dataset (sized to the time budget) rather than subsampling with a stride; the same pipeline went 0.0 -> 0.366 -> 0.380."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 890, "key": "meta/5dc2b841: A zero-score submission gives no diagnostic signal: the CSV validates, all datasets present, all columns corre", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "No format error was raised (the file was valid CSV, all columns correct, all datasets present), so it silently scored 0.0 with no diagnostic signal.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A zero-score submission gives no diagnostic signal: the CSV validates, all datasets present, all columns correct, and it silently returns 0.0 — so a local round-trip format check does NOT protect against it."}
