{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 894, "key": "meta/d390e9d6: At least one team hit Notebook Timeout on the scored rerun after completing in ~5.6h against the visible test ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Our submission notebook completes successfully in ~5.6h against the visible test clips, but the actual scored rerun came back as Notebook Timeout with no public score.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "At least one team hit Notebook Timeout on the scored rerun after completing in ~5.6h against the visible test clips; nobody (including the host) answered whether the rerun limit is the same 12h as Code Requirements states."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 895, "key": "meta/11c32623: The visible test set is deliberately minimal so notebooks verify in 15-30 minutes; the hidden test set swapped", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the visible verification dataset is intentionally kept minimal to allow rapid notebook saving and verification in 15-30 minutes. However ... the hidden test set swapped in during final evaluation ... is roughly the exact same size as the ~88 GB training dataset.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The visible test set is deliberately minimal so notebooks verify in 15-30 minutes; the hidden test set swapped in is approximately the size of the ~88 GB, 199-volume training set."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 896, "key": "meta/aad23cbb: Pip-installing packages at runtime breaks submission: the notebook is flagged as using the internet even after", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I keep getting a message saying my notebook is using the internet. I've disabled it and saved the changes, yet the notification telling me to disconnect the notebook from the internet keeps popping up\n--- These won't work during submission", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Pip-installing packages at runtime breaks submission: the notebook is flagged as using the internet even after internet is disabled; dependencies must be pre-staged as attached datasets."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 897, "key": "meta/4739566e: A pre-built CSV copied to submission.csv cannot work: the test folder is replaced by private samples at rerun,", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "pre built csv won't work, the test folder is replaced by private samples during submission. The submission file is expected to have nodes, edges from all the given datasets in the private test folder.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A pre-built CSV copied to submission.csv cannot work: the test folder is replaced by private samples at rerun, so dataset names must be discovered at runtime by globbing the input tree."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 898, "key": "meta/f44bb61a: A 7-submission diagnostic found 'Submission Scoring Error' is triggered by node timepoints exceeding a dataset", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "an earlier test with the same coordinate and topology extended to t=0 through t=9 (10 nodes, 9 edges) failed with Scoring Error. So the real trigger looks tied to the timepoint range ... submissions with t values beyond a dataset's actual frame count get rejected outright", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A 7-submission diagnostic found 'Submission Scoring Error' is triggered by node timepoints exceeding a dataset's real frame count, not by row count, topology, branching or coordinate values; the boundary was between t=5 (works) and t=9 (fails)."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 899, "key": "meta/9b8b8da3: Dynamic runtime discovery of test dataset names with zero edges scores successfully, giving a cheap structural", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I built a submission that discovers the test dataset names dynamically at runtime (globbing /kaggle/input/*/test/.zarr, no hardcoded names) and writes one node per dataset at t=0 with no edges at all ... yet it succeeded (score 0.000)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Dynamic runtime discovery of test dataset names with zero edges scores successfully, giving a cheap structural smoke-test submission that isolates format problems from scoring problems."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 900, "key": "meta/c99b7854: Public LB is reported as roughly 10% more optimistic than a held-out CV, with very large movie-to-movie varian", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the public LB is more optimistic by almost 10%. That being said, movie-to-movie variability is large: ±0.14, with 18% coefficient of variation. Worst movie scores 0.460 and the best is at 0.984. The public split might have more of the easy movies compared to my hold out set.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Public LB is reported as roughly 10% more optimistic than a held-out CV, with very large movie-to-movie variance: +/-0.14, 18% coefficient of variation, worst movie 0.460 and best 0.984."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 901, "key": "meta/ed553a9e: The public checkpoints were trained on all 199 annotated videos, so any CV using those weights on train videos", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The public weights were trained on all 199 annotated videos. Their split_manifest.json lists 199 under train, and the 40 in its own test list are all inside that same set. So if you're validating on train videos with those checkpoints, you're scoring the model on data it memorized.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The public checkpoints were trained on all 199 annotated videos, so any CV using those weights on train videos is scoring a memorised model."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 902, "key": "meta/5d227240: A training-set harness inverts the sign of post-processing ablations: a measured +0.0184 from disabling one co", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I ablated the post-processing in the public pipeline and measured +0.0184 from turning one stage off ... Submitted it and got 0.909 against my 0.912 baseline. The sign flipped ... A training-set harness will keep telling you to delete the components that matter most at test time.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A training-set harness inverts the sign of post-processing ablations: a measured +0.0184 from disabling one corrective stage became 0.909 vs a 0.912 baseline on LB."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 903, "key": "meta/ec02a26a: Multiple teams independently report that linker/motion-model improvements worth +0.012 to +0.04 on 5-fold CV c", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "My motion linker changes give around +0.012 on 5-fold CV on average, with no fold getting worse, but the LB gain is exactly +0.001.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Multiple teams independently report that linker/motion-model improvements worth +0.012 to +0.04 on 5-fold CV convert to exactly +0.001 on the public LB."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 904, "key": "meta/4822e345: The 0.946-class public notebook scores ~0.015 WORSE than a private 0.942 notebook under the same 5-fold local ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I also compared the public 0.946 LB notebook with my older private 0.942 LB notebook under the same 5-fold CV setup, and surprisingly the public one was about 0.015 worse locally.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The 0.946-class public notebook scores ~0.015 WORSE than a private 0.942 notebook under the same 5-fold local CV - direct evidence of public-test overfitting in the shared public lineage."}
