{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 906, "key": "meta/f49b21f6: The one concrete anti-shakeup discipline proposed in the shakeup thread is to decompose CV into edge_jaccard, ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "it is not useful to state/anayse \" 0.96 CV \"\nyou should break it down:\nedge_jaccard = ???\nadjusted_edge_jaccard = ???\nnode recall = ...\nestimated no of nodes = ...\ndivision = ...\nbreaks in tracks ....\nlink to wrong trajectory ....", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The one concrete anti-shakeup discipline proposed in the shakeup thread is to decompose CV into edge_jaccard, adjusted_edge_jaccard, node recall, node count, division jaccard, track breaks and mislinks rather than report a single number."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 907, "key": "meta/94d3f35d: Leave-one-embryo-out is the community-consensus CV, but it requires training your own detector because every r", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Leave-one-embryo-out is the right call, though as Adarsh says it means training your own model, since the released checkpoints have seen everything.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Leave-one-embryo-out is the community-consensus CV, but it requires training your own detector because every released checkpoint has seen both embryos."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 908, "key": "meta/06fc0c93: An exact public-LB split of the two score terms costs ONE submission: summarise() drops the division term when", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "summarise() drops the division term entirely when a submission contains no divisions at all (score = edge_jaccard if not has_divisions). So a fork-free submission returns your pure adjusted edge Jaccard, and the division term follows by subtraction", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "An exact public-LB split of the two score terms costs ONE submission: summarise() drops the division term when a submission contains no divisions, so a fork-free submission returns pure adjusted edge Jaccard."}
