{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 966, "key": "meta/1d55ca9e: UNTAKEN-ON-LB IDEA with concrete hyperparameters: a positive-unlabelled-aware weighted BCE answers the 2.82% s", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "GT is a sparse subset of the real nuclei, so the loss is positive-unlabelled-aware: GT centres are stamped as Gaussian positives (high weight), clearly-dark voxels are negatives (weight 1), and everything ambiguous/bright-but-unlabelled is ignored (weight 0.05) instead of penalised.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "UNTAKEN-ON-LB IDEA with concrete hyperparameters: a positive-unlabelled-aware weighted BCE answers the 2.82% sparsity problem directly - GT centres stamped as Gaussian positives at weight 12, clearly-dark voxels negatives at weight 1, and ambiguous bright-but-unlabelled voxels IGNORED at weight 0.05 rather than penalised."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 967, "key": "meta/b8d0ee67: That PU loss uses GAUSS_SIGMA=1.0, POS_THRESH=0.05, BG_Q=0.40 and W_POS/W_BG/W_IGN = 12.0/1.0/0.05, on XY-pool", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "GAUSS_SIGMA = 1.0; POS_THRESH = 0.05; BG_Q = 0.40\nW_POS, W_BG, W_IGN = 12.0, 1.0, 0.05\n ... The full 40-epoch / 171-movie run reproduces the submitted weights (`val_recall≈0.65`, public LB 0.841).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "That PU loss uses GAUSS_SIGMA=1.0, POS_THRESH=0.05, BG_Q=0.40 and W_POS/W_BG/W_IGN = 12.0/1.0/0.05, on XY-pooled x4 near-isotropic 64^3 inputs normalised p50->p99.5, reaching val_recall~0.65 and public LB 0.841 over 40 epochs on 171 movies."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 968, "key": "meta/925b31f3: This is one of the few public training setups with a leak-free split: the 4 public-LB movies are never trained", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Leak-free, embryo-grouped splits: the 4 public-LB movies are never trained on; validation movies are held out from both embryos for honest early-stopping on peak-recall.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "This is one of the few public training setups with a leak-free split: the 4 public-LB movies are never trained on and validation movies are held out from BOTH embryos, giving honest early-stopping on peak recall."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 969, "key": "meta/6ebe13ca: OPS TRAP: some Kaggle GPUs (P100 / sm_60) are incompatible with the bundled torch and fail only on a real CUDA", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "device (robust: some Kaggle\n# GPUs — e.g. P100/sm_60 — are incompatible with the bundled torch and only fail on a real launch)\nDEVICE = \"cpu\"\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    try:\n        _ = (torch.zeros(1, device=\"cuda\") + 1).cpu(); DEVICE = \"cuda\"", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "OPS TRAP: some Kaggle GPUs (P100 / sm_60) are incompatible with the bundled torch and fail only on a real CUDA launch, not on torch.cuda.is_available(), so a device probe must actually run a tensor op before committing to cuda."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 970, "key": "meta/58a8a561: Zarr v3 robustness pattern worth adopting: read .zarr and .geff through zarr with a hand-rolled blosc2 / manua", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Images are read via `zarr` with a hand-rolled blosc2 fallback; the GT only needs the node coordinates (`t,z,y,x`), read via `zarr` with a manual v3-chunk fallback (works even if the runtime ships Zarr v2, which cannot open these stores).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Zarr v3 robustness pattern worth adopting: read .zarr and .geff through zarr with a hand-rolled blosc2 / manual v3-chunk fallback, so the pipeline still works if the rerun runtime ships Zarr v2, which cannot open these stores at all."}
