{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 973, "key": "meta/c2850962: CONFIRMED IN THE PATCHED SCORER: sleepymegacat's Fact 4 is correct - the live code drops edges not connecting ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Drop edges that do not connect consecutive frames, i.e. keep only edges where\n    # t_target == t_source + 1. This removes backward-in-time edges (t_target <= t_source)\n    # and any edge spanning more than a single time step (t_target - t_source > 1).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CONFIRMED IN THE PATCHED SCORER: sleepymegacat's Fact 4 is correct - the live code drops edges not connecting consecutive frames before counting, removing backward edges and any edge spanning more than one time step, so they are neither TP nor FP."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 974, "key": "meta/9560b0b0: That dt==1 filter is ABSENT from the pre-patch scorer and was added by the 2026-07-17 patch, so any local vali", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "62c62,148\n<     node_attrs = graph.node_attrs(attr_keys=[td.DEFAULT_ATTR_KEYS.NODE_ID, td.DEFAULT_ATTR_KEYS.MATCHED_NODE_ID])", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "That dt==1 filter is ABSENT from the pre-patch scorer and was added by the 2026-07-17 patch, so any local validation or notebook calibrated before that date scores gap edges differently from the live metric."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 975, "key": "meta/0c3e1247: The node-count penalty formula is IDENTICAL in the patched and pre-patch scorers - max(0, edge_jaccard * (1 - ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "adj_edge_jaccard = max(\n            0.0, edge_jaccard * (1 - ADJUSTMENT_ALPHA * total_node_ratio),\n        )", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The node-count penalty formula is IDENTICAL in the patched and pre-patch scorers - max(0, edge_jaccard * (1 - 0.1 * total_node_ratio)) with no upper clip - so zhincez's offline replica was correct and their LB loss was a label-sparsity effect, not a scorer mismatch."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 976, "key": "meta/24a09a9f: The dt==1 drop in the patched scorer is the mechanism behind the reported exact-0.0 submissions: a stride-subs", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "An edge between non-consecutive frames can never match a GT edge under the official metric, so every single edge I submitted was structurally unmatchable — TP=0 across the board, regardless of detection quality.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 76, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "meta-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The dt==1 drop in the patched scorer is the mechanism behind the reported exact-0.0 submissions: a stride-subsampled pipeline emits only non-consecutive edges, every one is filtered out before counting, and TP is structurally zero with no error raised."}
