{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1071, "key": "swp/776e8d00: MEASURED division_jaccard #6: exactly 0.000, structurally, for any one-to-one linker - 40 FN out of 40 in a co", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A Hungarian linker forfeits the whole division term by construction. One successor per cell means no node ever has two outgoing edges, so division Jaccard is exactly 0.000 — in my test, 40 FN out of 40 — and 0.1 of the available 1.1 is gone before the tracker sees an image.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED division_jaccard #6: exactly 0.000, structurally, for any one-to-one linker - 40 FN out of 40 in a controlled test. One successor per cell means no node ever has out-degree 2. This is the largest single block of score most baselines leave on the table: 0.1 of the available 1.1."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1072, "key": "swp/b7ef4aa7: So the measured division_jaccard distribution across everyone who has published a number is 0.000, 0.0004, 0.0", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "adjusted_edge_jaccard plateaus around ~0.90–0.91 ... division_jaccard ≈ 0 for essentially everyone under the patch. Yet the post-patch top is 0.914–0.929, so the separation comes from somewhere.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "So the measured division_jaccard distribution across everyone who has published a number is 0.000, 0.0004, 0.03, 0.12, ~0.2, 0.22 - which supports the thesis that the plateau-to-podium gap (0.9465 -> 0.970 = 0.0235, i.e. division_jaccard ~= 0.235 at 0.1 weight) is dominated by the division term, though the 739686 node-count result shows the edge multiplier is a competing explanation for scores in the 0.95 band."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1073, "key": "swp/75cdcf0b: BEST DIVISION GEOMETRY IN THE FORUM, measured on LABELS not predictions (73 files, 36 divisions, 25,661 contin", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "continuation\n25,661\n1.724\n0.908 to 2.188\n3.350\n6.906\n18.692\n\ndivision step\n72\n4.569\n3.300 to 6.214\n7.081\n10.619\n12.336\n\nsister separation\n36\n8.849\n7.196 to 10.235\n11.866\n13.896\n14.653", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "BEST DIVISION GEOMETRY IN THE FORUM, measured on LABELS not predictions (73 files, 36 divisions, 25,661 continuation edges): continuation step median 1.724 um (IQR 0.908-2.188, p99 6.906); division step median 4.569 um (IQR 3.300-6.214, p90 7.081); sister separation median 8.849 um (IQR 7.196-10.235)."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1074, "key": "swp/87c4a476: THE DECISIVE NEGATIVE RESULT FOR GEOMETRY: a distance gate cannot isolate divisions because the division IQR s", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "5 um\n722\n30\n24:1\n\n7 um\n241\n8\n30:1\n\n9 um\n82\n3\n27:1\n\n10 um\n38\n1\n38:1\n\nThe division IQR sits entirely inside the ordinary continuation range, whose p99 is 6.91. A gate wide enough to admit the median division admits hundreds of continuations for every division it catches. The failure is a base rate", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE DECISIVE NEGATIVE RESULT FOR GEOMETRY: a distance gate cannot isolate divisions because the division IQR sits entirely inside the ordinary continuation range. At a 5 um gate the ratio of continuations to division steps is 24:1; at 7 um it is 30:1; at 9 um 27:1; at 10 um 38:1. The failure is a base rate, not an overlap you can tune away."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1075, "key": "swp/171ef7e2: SUPERSEDES EARLIER FORUM NUMBERS: the widely-cited 8.47 um parent-daughter step and 10.22 um sister separation", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "On seven divisions the longest parent to daughter step per event reads median 6.36 um and max 7.37 um on the labels, but median 8.47 um and max 13.65 um between the predicted nodes matched to them. That gap is detector localisation. ... so that ratio was meaningless.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "SUPERSEDES EARLIER FORUM NUMBERS: the widely-cited 8.47 um parent-daughter step and 10.22 um sister separation were measured between PREDICTED nodes and are dominated by detector localisation error, not cell motion. On labels the same events read median 6.36 um and max 7.37 um. The author retracted his own earlier ratio as meaningless. Tune a division gate on predicted positions and you calibrate your detector error."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1076, "key": "swp/3e1cb64f: Sister separation is the only quantity that genuinely separates (8.85 um vs 1.72 um), but it is a property of ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Sister separation is the one quantity that does look different, median 8.85 um against 1.72 um. But it is a property of a candidate pair rather than of an edge, so you can only use it after proposing the pair, and proposing pairs is the expensive step.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Sister separation is the only quantity that genuinely separates (8.85 um vs 1.72 um), but it is a property of a candidate PAIR, so it can only be applied after the pair is proposed - and proposing pairs is the expensive step. This is the precise statement of why division recall is hard."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1077, "key": "swp/59abdbff: CEILING ON CANDIDATE GRAPHS: a nearest-parent candidate graph at R~9.9 um, K<=10 covers only ~88% of the 151 G", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "on the training set, a simple nearest-parent candidate graph (R≈9.9µm, K≤10) only reaches ~88% coverage on the 151 GT division forks, versus ~99.7% on plain continuation edges", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CEILING ON CANDIDATE GRAPHS: a nearest-parent candidate graph at R~9.9 um, K<=10 covers only ~88% of the 151 GT division forks versus ~99.7% of plain continuation edges - a measurable gap concentrated on divisions before any classifier is involved."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1078, "key": "swp/4d884dd1: GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #1: missed divisions are not random - they concentrate almost entirely in crowded frames", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "bright thin lines at time t are new cell divisions that happen before t (maybe a few frames before). It is very good clue to detect division\n\ni think many cell divisions are not annotated in the Kaggle data.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #1: missed divisions are not random - they concentrate almost entirely in crowded frames (~3x the node count of recovered ones) and each failure trips 2 or 3 checks simultaneously, so loosening any single threshold recovers nothing and only adds false positives."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1079, "key": "swp/1df9941e: GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #2: the public 0.938-family pipeline runs a motion-relink stage that rebuilds the edge l", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "In the public 0.938 pipeline family the motion-relink stage rebuilds the edge list from a one-to-one Hungarian assignment before safe-div runs, so every fork the ILP produced is destroyed there. If you inherit that post-processing, any division work upstream of it is invisible.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #2: the public 0.938-family pipeline runs a motion-relink stage that rebuilds the edge list from a one-to-one Hungarian assignment BEFORE its safe-div step, destroying every fork the upstream ILP produced. Any team that inherited that post-processing has made all upstream division work invisible."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1080, "key": "swp/e09d603f: GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #3: an APPEARANCE cue for divisions that nobody in the corpus has operationalised - brig", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Hi! Yes you are free to use the data and all resources in Zebrahub for this competition! There is no overlap with the test set.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #3: an APPEARANCE cue for divisions that nobody in the corpus has operationalised - bright thin lines visible at time t mark divisions that happened a few frames earlier. The same competitor asserts many real divisions are simply not annotated in the Kaggle GT, and that they cluster (divisions are not isolated events)."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1081, "key": "swp/3637ead1: GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #4: an author of the official HOCT paper is in the forum with released inference code an", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The tracks are algorithm-generated, not manually curated. The *_tracks.csv lineages were produced with Ultrack ... they carry Ultrack's own systematic biases and error modes, especially around cell divisions and densely packed regions.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "GAP NOBODY IS WORKING #4: an author of the official HOCT paper is in the forum with released inference code and pretrained weights and states the team has never tried it on the competition data. One competitor who did try it reports it under-performs a tuned ILP, over-links, produces spurious forks rather than real divisions, and runs ~45 min/movie - but attributes that to feeding it uniform synthetic ball masks instead of real instance morphology, i.e. the approach is untested with proper segmentation input."}
