{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1083, "key": "swp/5615ebf4: CAVEAT ON ZEBRAHUB that changes how it should be used: its *_tracks.csv lineages are Ultrack-generated pseudo-", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "I got tired of trying to train a division model on ~304 events, so I built a synthetic dataset and I'm releasing it free (CC0). ... 165,267 labelled divisions across 4,056,226 nodes\n\nThat is roughly 540x more mitosis supervision", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CAVEAT ON ZEBRAHUB that changes how it should be used: its *_tracks.csv lineages are Ultrack-generated pseudo-labels, not manual curation, carrying Ultrack's systematic error modes ESPECIALLY AROUND DIVISIONS and in dense regions; only small subsets were manually corrected. Its imaging setup also differs from the competition data, so domain adaptation is needed. Training a division model on Zebrahub divisions means learning Ultrack's division errors."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1084, "key": "swp/f3652f94: CELL TRACKING CHALLENGE: usable, with a rules wrinkle. CTC terms require explicit per-user permission from the", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The division rate is deliberately inflated (4.07% of nodes vs ~0.26% in reality). A model starved of examples never learns mitosis. ... Nucleus texture and contrast are the weakest axes.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CELL TRACKING CHALLENGE: usable, with a rules wrinkle. CTC terms require explicit per-user permission from the CTC organisers; one competitor obtained it by email for himself, conditional on citation in the solution description. That is arguably not 'equally accessible to all Participants' unless each team repeats the request - though the host points everyone at CTC in the official welcome post, which is strong evidence the organisers consider it in-bounds."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1085, "key": "swp/f94273eb: THE SYNTHETIC DIVISION DATASET IS REAL, and the author claims CC0 with 165,267 labelled divisions across 4,056", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The official pipeline downsamples XY by 4 with a stride (vol[:, ::4, ::4]), not a block mean. ... A classical DoG detector recovers ~0.89 of the synthetic nuclei in a moderately dense field, ~0.76 when crowded; on the real annotated nuclei it recovers 0.91-0.94.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE SYNTHETIC DIVISION DATASET IS REAL, and the author claims CC0 with 165,267 labelled divisions across 4,056,226 nodes - roughly 540x the mitosis supervision in the competition ground truth."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1086, "key": "swp/645a27b1: BUT IT IS NOT A KAGGLE DATASET. Both links the author gives are /code/ notebook URLs. https://www.kaggle.com/d", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Dataset + full generator source (open, nothing hidden):\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/josefreitasalvesneto/biohub-synthetic-dataset", "review_after": null, "source_id": 77, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "sweep-forum", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "BUT IT IS NOT A KAGGLE DATASET. Both links the author gives are /code/ notebook URLs. https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/josefreitasalvesneto/biohub-synthetic-dataset returns HTTP 404; the /code/ URL returns 200. So the 18.5 GB is a NOTEBOOK OUTPUT, and the CC0 claim is a forum assertion by the author, not a Kaggle-enforced dataset licence field. It qualifies as public and free, but its availability depends on that notebook staying published."}
