{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1112, "key": "THE_DECOMPOSITION_plateau_already_has_divisions", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "adj_edge_jaccard 0.9260, division_jaccard 0.2308 (tp/fp/fn = 3/1/9)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 1291, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE CORRECTION THAT MATTERS MOST. From sjlee101/biohub-lf-dctta's OWN kernel output (ppsweep_results.csv, validator_results.csv): adj_edge_jaccard 0.9260, division_jaccard 0.2308 (tp/fp/fn = 3/1/9). 0.926 + 0.1*0.2308 = 0.9491, matching their 0.947 LB. So the public plateau is NOT edge 0.945 + divJ ~0 as I assumed all session - it is edge ~0.926 + divJ ~0.231. The plateau ALREADY has divisions working at roughly the level I computed for rank 1. Headroom is almost exactly EQUAL between the two terms: edge +0.0744, division +0.0769. CAVEAT: their CV is division-ENRICHED by construction (8 held-out samples each chosen to contain a GT division), so 0.2308 is an optimistic bound on the true test divJ."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1113, "key": "divisions_are_frozen_while_everyone_tunes_edges", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "their eight-config sweep leaves divJ pinned at exactly 0.2308 in seven of eight configs", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The reason divisions remain the better lever despite the plateau already scoring 0.231: their eight-config post-process sweep leaves divJ PINNED at exactly 0.2308 in seven of eight configs - every knob the field tunes moves only the edge term. Divisions are frozen, not absent. Mechanism: with the pack's default division_weight=1.0 and edge_weight=-1.0 a split earns exactly the same net ILP objective as a plain continuation, so the top tier sets ILP_DIVISION_WEIGHT=1.2 - strictly MORE expensive than continuation - then bolts divisions back on in a post-process filter cascade where every stage subtracts and none can propose. Measured cost: 111 safe divisions inserted across 8 embryos yield 3 TP."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1114, "key": "0.9465_is_the_honest_public_ceiling", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "the 0.966 submission ships 244 nodes at t=-1000 with -10000 coordinates and a hub of out-degree 2598", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "COMPLETE CENSUS of the >=0.95 tier: all 10 notebooks above 0.95 in the entire competition are exploit-contaminated, 100%. Verified at OUTPUT level, not by grep - the 0.966 submission ships 244 nodes at t=-1000 with -10000 coordinates and a hub of out-degree 2598, while the 0.947 submission has tmin=0 and max out-degree exactly 2. So 0.9465 IS the honest public ceiling and the entire visible frontier above it is one copy-pasted post-process cell. Nobody has combined the best honest pipeline WITH the exploit: all ten are the stripped-down support-pack baseline (~0.89 base + big hack), none enables the DeepCenter veto or safe-division gates the 0.947 family uses."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1115, "key": "score_tier_to_technique_map", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "0.912->0.940 (+0.028) is a single env-var edit ... 0.940->0.947 (+0.007) is three flags", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "SCORE TIER -> TECHNIQUE. <0.15 percentile-90 threshold + connected components + 15um NN (the official starter). 0.62-0.77 classical DoG/local-max + physical NMS + um-gated two-pass Hungarian - HARD CEILING ~0.77, nothing classical crosses 0.80. 0.81-0.86 learned detector OR tuned ILP but neither TTA nor centre-prior veto. 0.886-0.898 raw support pack (UNet+transformer+ILP+safe divisions). 0.908-0.912 + DeepCenter veto + D4 TTA. 0.940-0.947 + bidirectional harmonic fusion, adaptive short-track rescue, widened safe-div gates, in-notebook CV sweep. Two precise deltas: 0.912->0.940 (+0.028) is a SINGLE ENV-VAR EDIT (harmonic fusion on, short-track rescue on, safe-div gates 4.66/8.5->9.0/14.0, DeepCenter veto on, det 0.96875->0.965); 0.940->0.947 (+0.007) is THREE FLAGS. The whole 0.940-0.947 band is one codebase with different BIOHUB_* values."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1116, "key": "trackastra_handles_divisions_natively", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "a frame-pair Hungarian cannot fork", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "PROMISING AND ABSENT FROM THE TOP TIER: Trackastra (ECCV 2024, ISBI 2024 Cell Tracking Challenge winner) is a graph transformer that handles divisions NATIVELY. One notebook uses it but is bottlenecked by classical DoG detection at 0.616 - it has NEVER been paired with the support-pack detector. Its author names the exact structural reason the top tier is stuck: a frame-pair Hungarian cannot fork."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1117, "key": "CONTRADICTION_estimated_number_of_nodes_on_test", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "test ships no estimated_number_of_nodes", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "OPEN CONTRADICTION, must be settled before any node-count strategy. This agent reports 'test ships no estimated_number_of_nodes', which would make the node-count multiplier uncomputable at inference on the hidden set. The discussion agent reported the opposite - that T_true is readable at inference time from the GEFF metadata. Both cannot be true. RESOLVE by inspecting an actual test .zarr/.geff before betting anything on node-count calibration."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1118, "key": "only_one_independent_trainer_exists", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "31 of 65 notebooks attach the support pack, only one non-pilkwang weights dataset exists on the whole board", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Dependency census over 65 notebooks: 31 attach pilkwang's support pack and only ONE non-pilkwang weights dataset exists on the whole board. xiaoleilian is the sole independent trainer - a 3D U-Net from scratch on an explicit leak-free TRAIN-171/VAL-16 split, published as biohub-unet3d-weights - and it tops out at 0.884/0.843. So roughly 0.06 of public score is attributable to pilkwang's released weights alone."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1119, "key": "code/48d68d7c: The entire public 0.940-0.947 band is one identical codebase driven by BIOHUB_* environment variables; the who", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "os.environ[\"BIOHUB_VALIDATOR_N_PER_TYPE\"] = \"4\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_PPSWEEP_SELECT_MARGIN\"] = \"0.001\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_PPSWEEP_MAX_ADJ_LOSS\"] = \"0.0005\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_DEEPCENTER_TTA\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_SECONDARY_EDGE_FEATURE_TTA\"] = \"1\"", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The entire public 0.940-0.947 band is one identical codebase driven by BIOHUB_* environment variables; the whole +0.007 climb from 0.940 to 0.947 comes from three extra flags (post-process sweep validator, DeepCenter TTA, secondary edge-feature TTA), not from any modelling change."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1120, "key": "code/71bc616c: A second learned model, a 'DeepCenter' center-prior UNet3D from a separate dataset, is used purely as a VETO o", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "os.environ[\"BIOHUB_USE_DEEPCENTER_VETO\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_REQUIRE_DEEPCENTER_VETO\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_DEEPCENTER_GAP_VETO\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_DEEPCENTER_GAP_THRESHOLD\"] = \"0.25\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_DEEPCENTER_SAFE_DIV_VETO\"] = \"1\"", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "A second learned model, a 'DeepCenter' center-prior UNet3D from a separate dataset, is used purely as a VETO on gap-closes and on safe-division insertion in every 0.940+ notebook; it is a precision gate, not a detector."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1121, "key": "code/918d56d6: The 0.940+ family does attempt divisions, but only through a heavily capped 'safe division' post-link insertio", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "os.environ[\"BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_MAX_UM\"] = \"9.0\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_SISTER_MAX_UM\"] = \"14.0\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_SISTER_SYMMETRY_TAU\"] = \"0.6\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_FRAME_FRAC_CAP\"] = \"0.0076\"\nos.environ[\"BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_GLOBAL_FRAC_CAP\"] = \"0.00375\"", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The 0.940+ family does attempt divisions, but only through a heavily capped 'safe division' post-link insertion: at most 0.76% of a frame's nodes and 0.375% globally may become new division sources."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1122, "key": "code/52c4e628: kaiwalyaatulraut/biohub-solution is the only high-scoring notebook with a fully independent detector: its own ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "SCALE = np.array([1.625, 0.40625, 0.40625]); POOL = 4\nWEIGHT_NAMES = ['unet3d_bright.pt', 'unet3d_traintophat.pt']\nPREPROCS = ['', 'tophat']          # one per model; a model MUST use the preproc it was trained with\nREPAIR = True\nCAND_THR = 0.05", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "kaiwalyaatulraut/biohub-solution is the only high-scoring notebook with a fully independent detector: its own 2-model UNet3D ensemble (base=24) from a private weights dataset, differing preprocessing per model, with no support pack, no ILP and no learned edge scorer - association is pure constant-velocity Hungarian."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1123, "key": "code/e6c5ad2a: The independent kaiwalyaatulraut detector uses a far LOWER detection threshold (0.15, with a 0.05 candidate po", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "UNET_THRESH=0.15; NMS_UM=4.0\nDETECT_THRESH = min(UNET_THRESH, CAND_THR) if REPAIR else UNET_THRESH", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The independent kaiwalyaatulraut detector uses a far LOWER detection threshold (0.15, with a 0.05 candidate pool for repair) and a tighter 4.0 um NMS than the support-pack family's 0.965 threshold and 5.0 um NMS, showing two viable and opposite operating points."}
