{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1127, "key": "code/f31278f7: The originator of the support pack scores only 0.912 and 0.894 with his own notebooks, while downstream users ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "## Center Confirmation of Marginal Synthetic Gaps", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The originator of the support pack scores only 0.912 and 0.894 with his own notebooks, while downstream users of his weights reach 0.947 - so the +0.035 is entirely post-processing and TTA env-var tuning layered on his released artifacts."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1128, "key": "code/c4909be7: The exploit works because the scorer marks a predicted edge 'valid' only if its source or target matched a GT ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "pl.col(\"out_valid\").fill_null(False),\n        pl.col(\"in_valid\").fill_null(False),\n...\n    edge_attrs = edge_attrs.with_columns(\n        (pl.col(\"out_valid\") | pl.col(\"in_valid\")).alias(\"pred_valid\"),\n    )", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The exploit works because the scorer marks a predicted edge 'valid' only if its source or target matched a GT node (pred_valid = out_valid|in_valid, fill_null(False)), and only valid pred edges enter the edge-Jaccard denominator - so edges between fabricated unmatched nodes are completely invisible to the edge term, neither FP nor FN."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1129, "key": "code/04e19efa: Division FP is computed only over predicted dividing nodes that MATCHED a GT node, so any number of fabricated", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "if (\n            matched_pred.out_degree(pred_node) >= 2\n            and gt_graph.out_degree(gt_node) >= 1\n        ):\n            count += 1\n...\n    fp = max(0, matched_pred_divs - tp)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Division FP is computed only over predicted dividing nodes that MATCHED a GT node, so any number of fabricated forks at out-of-volume coordinates costs zero division FP; fp is additionally floored at max(0, matched_pred_divs - tp)."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1130, "key": "code/f5c39fa5: The hub node defeats division criterion 3 (all matched pred nodes in one weakly-connected component): linking ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "components = _weakly_connected_components(matched_pred, node_ids)\n...\n            if _has_stage_coverage(comp_attrs, gt_div, div_node):\n                div_candidates |= visited & pred_div_nodes\n        candidates[div_node] = div_candidates\n\n    pairing = _bipartite_max_matching(list(candidates), candidates)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The hub node defeats division criterion 3 (all matched pred nodes in one weakly-connected component): linking a single hub to every track root merges the whole prediction into one component, and the component's 'visited' set then donates every fabricated dividing node to the bipartite matching that awards division TPs."}
