{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1138, "key": "code/e5469ecc: The edge model DOES structurally permit divisions - the training loss softmaxes over the source axis so one pa", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "probs = torch.softmax(logits, dim=0)  # dim=0 intentional: divisions allowed, merges aren't\n...\n    max_children_per_node : int\n        Maximum number of outgoing edges per node (1 = no divisions, 2 = divisions allowed).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The edge model DOES structurally permit divisions - the training loss softmaxes over the source axis so one parent may have many children while merges are forbidden - and the ILP supports max_children_per_node=2, so the missing divisions are lost downstream, not in the model."}
