{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1174, "key": "code/b6d9a94b: Detection threshold is the most disputed single number on the board and nobody validates it per embryo: the re", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "**Detection threshold never validated.** `det_threshold=0.99` is inherited from the reference notebook and applied uniformly to every video - regardless of how dense or sparse that particular embryo is. The metric explicitly penalises over-predicting the total node count, which means a single global threshold is a poor fit when one sample has ~76 cells per frame and another has ~750.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Detection threshold is the most disputed single number on the board and nobody validates it per embryo: the reference notebook uses 0.99, the 0.940+ family 0.965, the 0.912 config 0.96875, and the independent line 0.15 on a differently-normalised heatmap - with one author noting one sample has ~76 cells per frame and another ~750."}
