{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1179, "key": "code/64000310: The most rigorous division work in the public set measures real GT division geometry and reports that the prev", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "- `BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_SISTER_MAX_UM` 12 -> **14 um** (daughter-to-daughter). GT sister separations reach 13.7 um (median 10.4, p90 13.0); the 12 um cap rejected ~29% of real divisions. Alone: `sismax14` = LB 0.939.\n- `BIOHUB_SAFE_DIV_MAX_UM` 7 -> **9 um** (parent-to-daughter). GT parent-daughter links reach 10.4 um; the 7 um cap rejected ~25% of real links.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The most rigorous division work in the public set measures real GT division geometry and reports that the previously standard caps were slicing off genuine divisions: GT sister separations reach 13.7 um (median 10.4, p90 13.0) so a 12 um cap rejected ~29% of real divisions, and GT parent-daughter links reach 10.4 um so a 7 um cap rejected ~25% of real links. The notebook reports each widening worth only +0.001 LB on its own."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "id": 1180, "key": "code/8c0aee0d: Recovering a claimed 25-29% of geometrically-excluded divisions buys only +0.002 LB, which bounds how much of ", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Each is already worth **+0.001** on the leaderboard on its own (0.938 -> 0.939)... This kernel tests whether the two +0.001 effects **stack** (target 0.940).", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Recovering a claimed 25-29% of geometrically-excluded divisions buys only +0.002 LB, which bounds how much of the missing division term is reachable by widening geometric gates alone and points the remaining ~0.07 of division headroom at the association stage rather than the post-process filter."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "id": 1181, "key": "code/4a96b899: The top tier's division post-process is a filter cascade, not a detector: a safe-div geometric proposer, a Dee", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "4. **Division post-processing** - a `safe-div` rule proposes divisions the ILP missed, a `DeepCenter` model vetoes false positives, and a **sister-symmetry gate** rejects divisions whose two daughters are implausibly asymmetric.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "code-scored", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The top tier's division post-process is a filter cascade, not a detector: a safe-div geometric proposer, a DeepCenter model veto, a sister-symmetry gate at tau=0.6, mutual-NN and a divergence gate - every stage subtracts candidates, none of them can propose a division the geometry missed."}
