{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "high", "id": 1183, "key": "north_star_0980_RECOMPUTED", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "adj_edge_jaccard 0.9260, division_jaccard 0.2308", "review_after": null, "source_id": 78, "status": "superseded", "superseded_by": 1291, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "NORTH STAR 0.980, recomputed on the real decomposition. The plateau is adj_edge ~0.926 + 0.1*divJ 0.231 = 0.947. Routes to 0.980, which needs +0.033: (a) divisions alone -> divJ 0.54, more than doubling the best measured value; (b) edge alone -> adj_edge 0.957, i.e. cutting the 60 edge errors per embryo to ~24; (c) BOTH, e.g. edge 0.940 + divJ 0.40 = 0.980. (c) is the only credible route. Rank 1's 0.970 needs edge 0.947 at their divJ, or a similar split. Headroom is near-equal - edge +0.074, division +0.077 - but divisions are the better lever because the field's post-process sweeps leave divJ frozen at 0.2308 across seven of eight configs while every knob moves the edge term."}
