{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1185, "key": "RESOLVED_test_ships_no_geff", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "test members: 408 / test .geff members: 0", "review_after": null, "source_id": 63, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "RESOLVED by direct inspection of the competition archive. The test split contains 408 members and ZERO .geff members - only .zarr volumes. estimated_number_of_nodes exists ONLY in train geff zarr.json metadata. So T_true is NOT readable at inference on the hidden set: any node-count calibration must ESTIMATE it from image statistics, it cannot be looked up. This resolves the contradiction between the two agents in favour of the code-scored agent."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1186, "key": "p15_ablation_DECOMPOSED_forks_are_net_negative", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "p15 fork-free: adj_edge 0.8923, divJ 0.0000 (0/0/3) | P9 forks-on: adj_edge 0.8882, divJ 0.0000 (0/9/3)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 79, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "MEASURED, and it REFUTES the divJ~0.19 inference. Scored both submissions with the PATCHED scorer against the 4 visible-test datasets (byte-identical train copies, GT available). p15 fork-free: adj_edge 0.8923, divJ 0.0000 (tp/fp/fn 0/0/3). P9 forks-on: adj_edge 0.8882, divJ 0.0000 (tp/fp/fn 0/9/3). Enabling forks produced NINE false positives and ZERO true positives, and made the EDGE term WORSE by 0.0041. Net effect of our division machinery on this substrate: -0.0041. The LB delta 0.906->0.925 cannot be attributed to the division term."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1187, "key": "our_forks_land_in_the_wrong_place_too", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "divJ tp/fp/fn 0/9/3 across 4 datasets containing 3 GT divisions total", "review_after": null, "source_id": 79, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "Our own pipeline reproduces the public field's failure exactly: 9 forks emitted, 0 TP. This matches the public stack's 111 safe divisions yielding 3 TP. We are not an exception - our forks are also proposed in the wrong places. CAVEAT: these 4 datasets contain only 3 GT divisions between them, so the division term is measured on a very small sample; the edge-term delta (-0.0041) is the more reliable half."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1188, "key": "node_count_multiplier_observed_directly", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "44b6_0b24845f edgeJ 0.9038 adj 0.9397 N_pred 19794 vs n_total 32795", "review_after": null, "source_id": 79, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "The node-count multiplier visible in real data: on 44b6_0b24845f, N_pred 19,794 against n_total 32,795 (a 40% under-prediction) lifted edge_jaccard 0.9038 to adj_edge 0.9397 - a +0.036 bonus. On 6bba_05db0fb1, N_pred 70,460 against n_total 69,800 gave 0.8401 -> 0.8393, a small penalty. The multiplier is real and sizeable, and it is doing more for the score on that dataset than the entire division machinery does anywhere."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1189, "key": "RESOLVED_node_pruning", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "track 10% +0.0010 | track 40% -0.1035 | random 10% -0.1626", "review_after": null, "source_id": 80, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "RESOLVED BY EXPERIMENT. Swept two pruning strategies on the p15 submission with the patched scorer (baseline adj_edge 0.8923, N_pred 121,854 against summed n_total 134,712 = 0.905 of true). WHOLE-TRACK deletion, shortest first: 10% -> +0.0010, 25% -> -0.0172, 40% -> -0.1035. SCATTERED random-node deletion: 10% -> -0.1626, 25% -> -0.3670, 40% -> -0.5410. At the SAME 10% cut the two strategies differ by 0.164 of score. So WHICH nodes you remove is the entire story, exactly as hypothesised. BOTH prior claims were right about different things: our monolith's 'optimum is no pruning' holds - the best result here is +0.001, inside noise - while the competitor's 44.7%-neutral result does NOT reproduce on this substrate, because we already sit at 0.905 of T_true. The multiplier caps at 1.10, leaving at most +0.09 relative, and edge loss overtakes it immediately past ~10%."}
