{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 1193, "key": "exp1_divergence_persistence_is_real", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "grandchild separation t+2 median 13.656 | parent's own incoming step median 1.862 vs population 1.817", "review_after": null, "source_id": 82, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "EXP-1: sisters KEEP DIVERGING - separation goes from 10.570um at birth to 13.656um at t+2 (n=147, IQR 11.767-14.888). That is a usable discriminator. By contrast the parent's OWN incoming step is median 1.862um against a population median of 1.817um - statistically indistinguishable, confirming motion history is chance and should not be a feature."}
